ily":"Williams","given":"C."},{"family":"Winterton","given":"D."},{"family":"Wong","given":"K.M."},{"family":"Woodfield-Pascoe","given":"N."},{"family":"Woodman","given":"J."},{"family":"Wyatt","given":"L."},{"family":"Wynberg","given":"R."},{"family":"Zhang","given":"B.G."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",3,29]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020",9]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, the total number of wild plant species used for human food is of 5,538, and 3,649 species are used as animal food. Medicinal use is made of 21,695 plants for medicines (20,313) and social uses (1,321). Wild plants are also used as sources of fuel (1,621) and raw materials (11,365). The flora of China ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"cCcNeWV8","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(FOC, 2020)","plainCitation":"(FOC, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30353,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/7DIQAQCF"],"itemData":{"id":30353,"type":"speech","title":"The Flora of China (FOC)","URL":"http://www.iplant.cn/frps/jingji/2?page=2","author":[{"literal":"FOC"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} reports economic use of species from 301 plant families: 1,068 species used as food, 3,815 species of medicinal plants, 713 plants for feed (grass/honey source), 531 plant species used for fiber, 1,318 timber species, 1,296 species used for ornamental purposes and 989 species used for oil (essential oils, gums, gels) (accessed June 2020).   
      Reviews of additional datasets such as “The Plant List “(http://www.theplantlist.org/) ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"pYPPyB05","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(TPL, 2020)","plainCitation":"(TPL, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30351,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/CRWKEZND"],"itemData":{"id":30351,"type":"speech","title":"The Plant List","URL":"http://www.theplantlist.org/ (acessed November 2020)","author":[{"literal":"TPL"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, “World Flora Online” (http://www.worldfloraonline.org/) ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"wucqrkFG","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(WFO, 2020)","plainCitation":"(WFO, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30352,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/6QMXEMHR"],"itemData":{"id":30352,"type":"speech","title":"World Flora Online","URL":"http://www.worldfloraonline.org/(acessed Novemeber 2020)","author":[{"literal":"WFO"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} and the United States of America “Plant Germplasm System” (https://npgsweb.arsgrin.gov/gringlobal/taxon/ taxonomysearch) ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"yuMgFjqG","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(GRIN-WEP, 2020)","plainCitation":"(GRIN-WEP, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30350,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/TX534CB8"],"itemData":{"id":30350,"type":"speech","title":"GRIN-Global Species Data","URL":"https://npgsweb.ars-grin.gov/gringlobal/taxon/taxonomysearch","author":[{"family":"GRIN-WEP","given":""}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} were not possible in the same way because those databases are not searchable in a way that allows identification of wild species and uses across different regions of the globe.  
