      While general trends at global and regional scales can be identified, policy and practice pathways will lead most surely toward sustainable gathering in the future when they are context specific and build in the capacity for adaptation to changing conditions ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"3JMp1BDw","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Hart\\\\uc0\\\\u8208{}Fredeluces, 2021; Sinasson, 2021)","plainCitation":"(Hart?Fredeluces, 2021; Sinasson, 2021)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":19191,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/CJCBTM79"],"itemData":{"id":19191,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Journal of Ecology","issue":"3","language":"en","page":"1133–1147","title":"Simulated Indigenous fire stewardship increases the population growth rate of an understorey herb","volume":"109","author":[{"family":"Hart?Fredeluces","given":"G.M."},{"family":"Ticktin","given":"T."},{"family":"Lake","given":"F.K."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2021"]]}}},{"id":19223,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/NMMZLSFX"],"itemData":{"id":19223,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Global Ecology and Conservation","language":"en","page":"01527","title":"Ecological patterns and effectiveness of protected areas in the preservation of Mimusops species’ habitats under climate change","volume":"27","author":[{"family":"Sinasson","given":"G.K."},{"family":"Shackleton","given":"C.M."},{"family":"Teka","given":"O."},{"family":"Sinsin","given":"B."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2021"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Localized monitoring and assessment can supply appropriately scaled information ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"Q3ExP2t0","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Papageorgiou, 2020; Sinasson, 2021)","plainCitation":"(Papageorgiou, 2020; Sinasson, 2021)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1340,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/ZH3L9RVH"],"itemData":{"id":1340,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Journal of ethnobiology and ethnomedicine","DOI":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13002-020-00390-4","issue":"1","note":"publisher: BioMed Central","page":"1–23","title":"Local knowledge about sustainable harvesting and availability of wild medicinal plant species in Lemnos island, Greece","volume":"16","author":[{"family":"Papageorgiou","given":"Dimitrios"},{"family":"Bebeli","given":"Penelope J"},{"family":"Panitsa","given":"Maria"},{"family":"Schunko","given":"Christoph"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}},{"id":19223,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/NMMZLSFX"],"itemData":{"id":19223,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Global Ecology and Conservation","language":"en","page":"01527","title":"Ecological patterns and effectiveness of protected areas in the preservation of Mimusops species’ habitats under climate change","volume":"27","author":[{"family":"Sinasson","given":"G.K."},{"family":"Shackleton","given":"C.M."},{"family":"Teka","given":"O."},{"family":"Sinsin","given":"B."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2021"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} to support adaptation. Similarly, local-scale scenarios and models can inform policy and practice about possible futures for gathering ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"dhsNwI27","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Bond\\\\uc0\\\\u233{}, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Bondé, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":19174,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/6KJFBZI6"],"itemData":{"id":19174,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Biota Neotropica","language":"en","title":"Scenario-modelling for the sustainable management of non-timber forest products in tropical ecosystems","volume":"20","author":[{"family":"Bondé","given":"L."},{"family":"Assis","given":"J.C."},{"family":"Benavides-Gordillo","given":"S."},{"family":"Canales-Gomez","given":"E."},{"family":"Fajardo","given":"J."},{"family":"Marrón-Bec