      By the later 1990s and 2000s, some contributions to a growing debate in the academic literature about ecosystem effects of fishing became strident and even adversarial, as disagreements about specific benchmarks, and the effectiveness of measures taken to achieve them, were debated ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"nDBmbh1Y","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Corbin, 2002; Daan, 2011; Jaenike, 2007; Mora, 2009; Verweij, 2010; Wilberg & Miller, 2007; Worm, 2007; Worm & Myers, 2004)","plainCitation":"(Corbin, 2002; Daan, 2011; Jaenike, 2007; Mora, 2009; Verweij, 2010; Wilberg & Miller, 2007; Worm, 2007; Worm & Myers, 2004)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30376,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/2EEJWQMH"],"itemData":{"id":30376,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Canadian Journal of Conservation","language":"en","page":"7–32","title":"Silences and Lies: how the industrial fisheries constrained the voices of ecological conservation","volume":"27","author":[{"family":"Corbin","given":"C."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2002"]]}}},{"id":30385,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/FH6R459B"],"itemData":{"id":30385,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"ICES Journal of Marine Science","language":"en","page":"1375–1378","title":"Apocalypse in world fisheries? The reports of their death are greatly exaggerated","volume":"68","author":[{"family":"Daan","given":"N."},{"family":"Gislason","given":"H."},{"family":"Pope","given":"J.G."},{"family":"Rice","given":"J.C."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2011"]]}}},{"id":30408,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/PCKLWLVH"],"itemData":{"id":30408,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Science","language":"fr","page":"1285","title":"Comment on \\"Impacts of Biodiversity Loss on Ocean Ecosystem Services","volume":"316","author":[{"family":"Jaenike","given":"J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2007"]]}}},{"id":30389,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/BYFQPJYV"],"itemData"