ntegrity","URL":"https://ec.europa.eu/environment/marine/pdf/6-Task-Group-6.pdf","author":[{"family":"Rice","given":"J."},{"family":"Arvanitidis","given":"C."},{"family":"Borja","given":"A."},{"family":"Frid","given":"C."},{"family":"Hiddink","given":"J."},{"family":"Krause","given":""},{"family":"Lorance","given":"P."},{"family":"Ragnarsson","given":"Á"},{"family":"Sköld","given":"M."},{"family":"Trabucco","given":"B."}],"editor":[{"family":"Piha","given":"H."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2022",4,18]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, ecosystem processes ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"mTTq0shY","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Rogers, 2010)","plainCitation":"(Rogers, 2010)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30394,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/662PG2AF"],"itemData":{"id":30394,"type":"book","event-place":"Luxembourg","ISBN":"978-92-79-15656-4","language":"en","note":"page: 63","publisher":"Office for Official Publications of the European Communities","publisher-place":"Luxembourg","title":"Marine Strategy Framework Directive Task Group 4 Report: Food webs","URL":"https://ec.europa.eu/environment/marine/pdf/4-Task-group-4.pdf","author":[{"family":"Rogers","given":"S."},{"family":"Casini","given":"M."},{"family":"Cury","given":"P."},{"family":"Heath","given":"M."},{"family":"Irigoien","given":"X."},{"family":"Kuosa","given":"H."},{"family":"Scheidat","given":"M."},{"family":"Skov","given":"H."},{"family":"Stergiou","given":"K."},{"family":"Trenkel","given":"V."},{"family":"Wikner","given":"J."},{"family":"Yunev","given":"O."}],"editor":[{"family":"Piha","given":"H."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2022",4,18]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} and biodiversity including threatened species ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"j9CHx3Ww","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(S. K. J. Cochrane, 2010)","plainCitation":"(S. K. J. Cochrane, 2010)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30395,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/WX2VAXYV"],"itemData":{"id":30395,"type":"book","edition":"Office for Official Publications of the European Communities","event-place":"Luxembourg","ISBN":"978-92-79-15650-2","number-of-pages":"120","publisher-place":"Luxembourg","title":"Marine Strategy Framework Directive Task Group 1 Report: Biological Diversity","URL":"https://ec.europa.eu/environment/marine/pdf/1-Task-group-1-Report-on-Biological-Diversity.pdf","author":[{"family":"Cochrane","given":"S.K.J."},{"family":"Connor","given":"D.W."},{"family":"Nilsson","given":"P."},{"family":"Mitchell","given":"J.Reker"},{"family":"Franco","given":"J."},{"family":"Valavanis","given":"V."},{"family":"Moncheva","given":"S."},{"family":"Ekebom","given":"J."},{"family":"Nygaard","given":"K."},{"family":"Serrão Santos","given":"R."},{"family":"Narberhaus","given":"I."},{"family":"Packeiser","given":"T."},{"family":"Bund","given":"W.","non-dropping-particle":"van de"},{"family":"Cardoso","given":"A.C."}],"editor":[{"family":"Zampoukas","given":"N."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2022",4,18]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Subsidies and other economic harmful incentives were not mentioned in Aichi Biodiversity Target 6, but were addressed directly for all uses of biodiversity in Target 3.
      Conspicuously absent in the Aichi Biodiversity Target 6 was reference to social outcomes as part of sustainable fishing. Those aspects were all covered in a single Aichi Biodiversity Target 14, with general language for all uses of biodiversity that “by 2020, ecosystems that provide essential services, including services related to water, and contribute to health, livelihoods and well-being, are restored and safeguarded, taking into account the needs of women, indigenous and local communities, and the poor and vulnerable”. The implications of actions to promote implementation of Article 8j of the Convention on Biological Diversity were a topic of debate throughout the 10th Conference of the Parties, such that consensus on the necessity of specific social outcomes was not reached. 
      
 2.2.3.2.2 Post-2010
The methods for the review of post 2010 literature is available at 10.5281/zenodo.6472995. Table 2.1 presents the occurrence of the four traditional aspects of sustainable use in fishing in the over 400 papers considered for this analysis: the target species of the fishery, the ecosystem context in which the fishery occurred, the economic context and revenues from the fishery, and the social context in which the fishery occurred, supported livelihoods and distributed benefits. Comparable numbers of papers considered both the target species or species complex (126) and the ecosystem context in which the fishery occurred (117). Somewhat fewer papers considered the social context of the fishery (101) and fewer yet the economic context of fisheries (70). 
      Despite being the most common theme addressed, relatively little genuinely new thinking was presented about sustainable outcomes for the target species and species being incidentally harvested. Nearly half the papers presented new or revised methods for estimating the standard benchmarks for sustainable harvesting rates and/or sustainable levels of the populations being harvesting ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"yQ8NT711","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Barneche, 2018; Jusufovski & Kuparinen, 2020; Kindsvater, 2020; Lassen, 2013; Pilling, 2016; Vasilakopoulos, 2016; S. J. Zhou, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Barneche, 2018; Jusufovski & Kuparinen, 2020; Kindsvater, 2020; Lassen, 2013; Pilling, 2016; Vasilakopoulos, 2016; S. J. Zhou, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30686,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/NC3LKHII"],"itemData":{"id":30686,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Science","language":"en","page":"642–644","title":"Fish reproductive-energy output increases disproportionately with body size","volume":"360","author":[{"family":"Barneche","given":"D.R."},{"family":"Robertson","given":"D.R."},{"family":"White","given":"C.R."},{"family":"Marshall","given":"D.J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}}},{"id":30706,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/GHIYT3YH"],"itemData":{"id":30706,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Fisheries Research","language":"en","title":"Exploring individual and population eco-evolutionary feedbacks under the coupled effects of fishing and predation","volume":"231","author":[{"family":"Jusufovski","given":"D."},{"family":"Kuparinen","given":"A."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}},{"id":30705,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/QES5YC37"],"itemData":{"id":30705,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Fish and Fisheries","language":"en","page":"223–236","title":"The consequences of size-selective fishing mortality for larval production and sustainable yield in spec