      The ecosystem context for the sustainability of fishing had a lower proportion of papers (<30%) simply elaborating alternative benchmarks for sustainable impacts, whereas a comparable proportion expanded the notion of “sustainable use” to broader ecosystem properties. Some of these are related to the harvest strategies, such as balanced harvesting of all sizes of fish and invertebrates in a community in proportion to their relative abundances ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"Lh7RALDQ","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Garcia, 2016; Law, 2012, 2015; Plank, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Garcia, 2016; Law, 2012, 2015; Plank, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":34883,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/2T6PLIER"],"itemData":{"id":34883,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"ICES Journal of Marine Science","language":"en","page":"1668–1678","title":"Balanced harvesting in fisheries: a preliminary analysis of management implications","volume":"73","author":[{"family":"Garcia","given":"S.M."},{"family":"Rice","given":"J.C."},{"family":"Charles","given":"A."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}}},{"id":30523,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/EDGY5NQV"],"itemData":{"id":30523,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"ICES Journal of Marine Science","language":"en","page":"602–614","title":"On balanced exploitation of marine ecosystems: results from dynamic size spectra","volume":"69","author":[{"family":"Law","given":"R."},{"family":"Plank","given":"M.J."},{"family":"Kolding","given":"J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2012"]]}}},{"id":30524,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/MEA82SKS"],"itemData":{"id":30524,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Fish and fisheries","language":"en","page":"160–174","title":"Squaring the circle: reconciling fishing and conservation of aquatic ecosystems","volume":"16","author":[{"family":"Law","given":"R."},{"family":"Kolding","given":"J."},{"family":"Plank","given":"M.J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}}},{"id":34510,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/YYCWFH2N"],"itemData":{"id":34510,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Fish and Fisheries","DOI":"10.1111/faf.12172","ISSN":"14672960","issue":"2","journalAbbreviation":"Fish Fish","language":"en","page":"212-225","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Balanced harvesting can emerge from fishing decisions by individual fishers in a small-scale fishery","URL":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/faf.12172","volume":"18","author":[{"family":"Plank","given":"Michael J"},{"family":"Kolding","given":"Jeppe"},{"family":"Law","given":"Richard"},{"family":"Gerritsen","given":"Hans D"},{"family":"Reid","given":"David"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2022",3,22]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017",3]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Many were about the need to set harvesting benchmarks in the contexts of environmental dynamics, bringing climate change considerations directly into sustainable fishing. Only 15% of papers discussing sustainability of fishing in an ecosystem context addressed the social or economic aspects of fishing at the same time, with most of those dealing with ways to take into account the displacement of fisheries when applying spatial tools to protect some parts of the ecosystem from the impacts of fishing ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"2NTaCq7A","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Arkema, 2015; Cinner, 2019; Giron-Nava, 2019; Lowerre-Barbieri, 2019)","plainCitation":"(Arkema, 2015; Cinner, 2019; Giron-Nava, 2019; Lowerre-Barbieri, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30691,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/G37TDJS3"],"itemData":{"id":30691,"type":"paper-conference","container-title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences – USA","language":"en","page":"7390–7395","title":"Embedding ecosystem services in coastal planning leads to better outcomes for people and nature","volume":"112","author":[{"family":"Arkema","given":"K.K."},{"family":"Verutes","given":"G.M."},{"family":"Wood","given":"S.A."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}}},{"id":30696,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/BDHWL6AS"],"itemData":{"id":30696,"type":"paper-conference","container-title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences – USA","language":"en","page":"26474–26483","title":"Sixteen years of social and ecological dynamics reveal challenges and opportunities for adaptive management in sustaining the commons","volume":"116","author":[{"family":"Cinner","given":"J.E."},{"family":"Lau","given":"J.D."},{"family":"Bauman","given":"A.G."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}},{"id":30698,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/MZTED36Z"],"itemData":{"id":30698,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Fish and Fisheries","language":"en","page":"214–223","title":"Managing at Maximum Sustainable Yield does not ensure economic well-being for artisanal fishers","volume":"20","author":[{"family":"Giron-Nava","given":"A."},{"family":"Johnson","given":"A.F."},{"family":"Cisneros-Montemayor","given":"A.M."},{"family":"Aburto-Oropeza","given":"O."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}},{"id":30672,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/TJT9EUU8"],"itemData":{"id":30672,"type":"article-journal","abstract":"Abstract\\n            Marine resource management is shifting from optimizing single species yield to redefining sustainable fisheries within the context of managing ocean use and ecosystem health. In this introductory article to the theme set, “Plugging spatial ecology into ecosystem-based management (EBM)” we conduct an informal horizon scan with leaders in EBM research to identify three rapidly evolving areas that will be game changers in integrating spatial ecology into EBM. These are: (1) new data streams from fishers, genomics, and technological advances in remote sensing and bio-logging; (2) increased analytical power through “Big Data” and artificial intelligence; and (3) better integration of social dimensions into management. We address each of these areas by first imagining capacity in 20 years from now, and then highlighting emerging efforts to get us there, drawing on articles in this theme set, other scientific literature, and presentations/discussions from the symposium on “Linkages between spatial ecology and sustainable fisheries” held at the ICES Annual Science Conference in September 2017.","container-title":"ICES Journal of Marine Science","DOI":"10.1093/icesjms/fsy209","ISSN":"1054-3139, 1095-9289","issue":"2","language":"en","page":"467-476","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Preparing for the future: integrating spatial ecology into ecosystem-based management","title-short":"Preparing for the future","URL":"https://academic.oup.com/icesjms/article/76/2/467/5299619","volume":"76","author":[{"family":"Lowerre-Barbieri","given":"Susan K"},{"family":"Catalán","given":"Ignacio A"},{"family":"Frugård Opdal","given":"Anders"},{"family":"Jørgensen","given":"Christian"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2022",4,22]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019",4,1]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. 
