,"itemData":{"id":31792,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Fisheries research","ISSN":"0165-7836","journalAbbreviation":"Fisheries research","page":"59-70","title":"Combining sale records of landings and fishers knowledge for predicting métiers in a small-scale, multi-gear, multispecies fishery","volume":"195","author":[{"family":"Palmer","given":"Miquel"},{"family":"Tolosa","given":"Borja"},{"family":"Grau","given":"Antoni Maria"},{"family":"Mar Gil","given":"Maria","non-dropping-particle":"del"},{"family":"Obregón","given":"Clara"},{"family":"Morales-Nin","given":"Beatriz"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":368,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/JXDXL3RN"],"itemData":{"id":368,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Frontiers in Marine Science","DOI":"10.3389/fmars.2017.00106","issue":"APR","title":"Harvest strategies for an ecosystem approach to fisheries management in western Mediterranean demersal fisheries","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85020168102&doi=10.3389%2ffmars.2017.00106&partnerID=40&md5=36df8f404ec7c77962f689a7da5e64d0","volume":"4","author":[{"family":"Quetglas","given":"A."},{"family":"Merino","given":"G."},{"family":"González","given":"J."},{"family":"Ordines","given":"F."},{"family":"Garau","given":"A."},{"family":"Grau","given":"A.M."},{"family":"Guijarro","given":"B."},{"family":"Oliver","given":"P."},{"family":"Massutí","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. A small number of papers also cover exploitation of crustaceans ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"IO7k2tq2","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Carvalho, Vasconcelos, Pil\\\\uc0\\\\u243{}, Pereira, & Gaspar, 2017; A. Rivera, Gelcich, Garc\\\\uc0\\\\u237{}a-Fl\\\\uc0\\\\u243{}rez, & Acu\\\\uc0\\\\u241{}a, 2016; Antonella Rivera, Gelcich, Garc\\\\uc0\\\\u237{}a-Fl\\\\uc0\\\\u243{}rez, & Acu\\\\uc0\\\\u241{}a, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Carvalho, Vasconcelos, Piló, Pereira, & Gaspar, 2017; A. Rivera, Gelcich, García-Flórez, & Acuña, 2016; Antonella Rivera, Gelcich, García-Flórez, & Acuña, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":376,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/L5VUDIJC"],"itemData":{"id":376,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2017.01.008","page":"34-44","title":"Socio-economic, operational and technical characterisation of the harvesting of gooseneck barnacle (Pollicipes pollicipes) in SW Portugal: Insights towards fishery co-management","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85009170677&doi=10.1016%2fj.marpol.2017.01.008&partnerID=40&md5=7811606bf0e2b057b997b0e29ed391f9","volume":"78","author":[{"family":"Carvalho","given":"A.N."},{"family":"Vasconcelos","given":"P."},{"family":"Piló","given":"D."},{"family":"Pereira","given":"F."},{"family":"Gaspar","given":"M.B."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31781,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/83GSY46H"],"itemData":{"id":31781,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Ambio","DOI":"10.1007/s13280-015-0687-z","issue":"2","page":"230-240","title":"Assessing the sustainability and adaptive capacity of the gooseneck barnacle co-management system in Asturias, N. Spain","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84958103200&doi=10.1007%2fs13280-015-0687-z&partnerID=40&md5=f506dbfbd3232d883f84b2172d079bd5","volume":"45","author":[{"family":"Rivera","given":"A."},{"family":"Gelcich","given":"S."},{"family":"García-Flórez","given":"L."},{"family":"Acuña","given":"J.L."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}}},{"id":365,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/64CDWNTE"],"itemData":{"id":365,"type":"article-journal","abstract":"The Asturian gooseneck barnacle (Pollicipes pollicipes Gmelin, 1790) fishery has been managed through territorial use rights in fisheries (TURFs) since its inception >20 yrs ago. As part of this agreement, fishers are allotted exclusive extraction rights and active participation\\nin management strategies. In return for these rights, fishers are responsible for gathering data on effort and extraction in the fishery. We used the extensive time-series gathered by the fishers to assess the sustainability of the fishery. Additionally, we used survey techniques to explore\\nthe social-ecological drivers of this sustainability. The fishery has succeeded in maintaining or increasing catch per unit effort in all TURFs. Furthermore, the system has received public approval, where 73% of the stakeholders indicated that the only way to maintain a sustainable gooseneck\\nbarnacle fishery in Asturias is through the current management regime. The system has contributed to the sustainability of the fishery via: (1) creating a window of opportunity for management of the resource; (2) the continuous incorporation of scientific information and fishers' knowledge\\ninto management frameworks; (3) empowerment of the resource users; (4) embracing adaptive capacity through flexible management guidelines; and (5) matching management scales with the main life-history traits of the species. As in any dynamic system, the gooseneck barnacle fishery is currently\\nfaced with important challenges that might impact its sustainability, indicating that there are no simple recipes for fisheries management. Nonetheless, this system provides a set of basic principles for TURFs, which may be conducive to adaptive and sustainable fisheries.","container-title":"Bulletin of Marine Science","DOI":"10.5343/bms.2015.1080","issue":"1","journalAbbreviation":"Bulletin of Marine Science","page":"35-51","title":"Trends, drivers, and lessons from a long-term data series of the Asturian (northern Spain) gooseneck barnacle territorial use rights system","URL":"https://www.ingentaconnect.com/content/umrsmas/bullmar/2017/00000093/00000001/art00005","volume":"93","author":[{"family":"Rivera","given":"Antonella"},{"family":"Gelcich","given":"Stefan"},{"family":"García-Flórez","given":"Lucía"},{"family":"Acuña","given":"José Luis"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017",1,1]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, mollusks ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"LORz8Wbi","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Baeta, Breton, Ubach, & Ariza, 2018; Duncan, Brand, Strand, & Foucher, 2016; \\\\uc0\\\\u214{}ndes, Kaiser, & G\\\\uc0\\\\u252{}\\\\uc0\\\\u231{}l\\\\uc0\\\\u252{}soy, 2020; F. Pereira, Vasconcelos, Moreno, & Gaspar, 2019; P. Silva, Cabral, Rangel, Pereira, & Pita, 2019; Szostek, Murray, Bell, & Kaiser, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Baeta, Breton, Ubach, & Ariza, 2018; Duncan, Brand, Strand, & Foucher, 2016; Öndes, Kaiser, & Güçlüsoy, 2020; F. Pereira, Vasconcelos, Moreno, & Gaspar, 2019; P. Silva, Cabral, Rangel, Pereira, & Pita, 2019; Szostek, Murray, Bell, & Kaiser, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":370,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/YULEC7WK"],"itemData":{"id":370,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Ocean and Coastal Management","DOI":"10.1016/j.ocecoaman.2018.01.012","page":"143-154","title":"A socio-ecological approach to the declining Catalan clam fisheries","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85041434506&doi=10.1016%2fj.ocecoaman.2018.01.012&partnerID=40&md5=bb0511fa277fa86f86ceb212ad6d621a","volume":"154","author":[{"family":"Baeta","given":"M."},{"family":"Breton","given":"F."},{"family":"Ubach","given":"R."},{"family":"Ariza","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}}},{"id":31535,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/G25LWCTK"],"itemData":{"id":31535,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","collection-title":"Developments in Aquaculture and Fisheries Science","container-title":"Developments in Aquaculture and Fisheries Science","DOI":"10.1016/B978-0-444-62