w/master/csl-citation.json"}. Sometimes, in general terms, this fishing is more profitable than the large-scale fishing industry since costs are lower and catches are similar ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"EwQyjod0","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Almeida, Vaz, Cabral, & Ziegler, 2014)","plainCitation":"(Almeida, Vaz, Cabral, & Ziegler, 2014)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31800,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/ZAYFLGJM"],"itemData":{"id":31800,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"International Journal of Life Cycle Assessment","DOI":"10.1007/s11367-013-0646-5","issue":"2","page":"297-306","title":"Environmental assessment of sardine (Sardina pilchardus) purse seine fishery in Portugal with LCA methodology including biological impact categories","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84893732137&doi=10.1007%2fs11367-013-0646-5&partnerID=40&md5=ce9019d10306e79daa166fbcb5553987","volume":"19","author":[{"family":"Almeida","given":"C."},{"family":"Vaz","given":"S."},{"family":"Cabral","given":"H."},{"family":"Ziegler","given":"F."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. In some parts, the increase in the tourism industry and, less conspicuously, the increase in recreational fishing, led to a slight expansion in local economies ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"afn1lskao9","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Marengo, Culioli, Santoni, Marchand, & Durieux, 2015)","plainCitation":"(Marengo, Culioli, Santoni, Marchand, & Durieux, 2015)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31798,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/2BB3P5VE"],"itemData":{"id":31798,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Management and Ecology","DOI":"10.1111/fme.12110","issue":"3","page":"249-260","title":"Comparative analysis of artisanal and recreational fisheries for Dentex dentex in a Marine Protected Area","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84929265099&doi=10.1111%2ffme.12110&partnerID=40&md5=3d583f397f90edd8f42106c112c87d15","volume":"22","author":[{"family":"Marengo","given":"M."},{"family":"Culioli","given":"J.-M."},{"family":"Santoni","given":"M.-C."},{"family":"Marchand","given":"B."},{"family":"Durieux","given":"E.D.H."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} and generated new incomes and additional revenues in the form of concessions and permits ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a2m639ssua8","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(C. Antunes, 2015)","plainCitation":"(C. Antunes, 2015)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31782,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/C4RFSYFY"],"itemData":{"id":31782,"type":"chapter","container-title":"Freshwater Fisheries Ecology","event-place":"Oxford, UK","ISBN":"978-1-118-39442-7","note":"DOI: 10.1002/9781118394380.ch23","page":"268-282","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","publisher-place":"Oxford, UK","title":"Iberian inland fisheries","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84984844857&doi=10.1002%2f9781118394380.ch23&partnerID=40&md5=c6a7af8f3dd1d871e5423260a9b0aae9","author":[{"family":"Antunes","given":"C."},{"family":"Cobo","given":"F."},{"family":"Araújo","given":"M.J."}],"editor":[{"family":"Craig","given":"J.F."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. On the other hand, it is also well established in the literature that small-scale European fishing is threatened by the competition among different uses of aquatic resources and by decreasing profitability, detected in almost all systems evaluated ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"JTxDdZ5J","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(F. Maynou, 2014)","plainCitation":"(F. Maynou, 2014)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":34075,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/I6SD7P3S"],"itemData":{"id":34075,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Journal of Applied Ichthyology","DOI":"10.1111/jai.12460","issue":"5","page":"978-985","title":"Bio-economic analysis of the Mar Menor (Murcia, SE Spain) small-scale lagoon fishery","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84908251441&doi=10.1111%2fjai.12460&partnerID=40&md5=de31f1e791a98aca1cd7ebfa70c485f8","volume":"30","author":[{"family":"Maynou","given":"F."},{"family":"Martínez-Baños","given":"P."},{"family":"Demestre","given":"M."},{"family":"Franquesa","given":"R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. 
	When European small-scale fishing systems are analyzed, the majority of the papers describe activities that are still profitable ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"i470X8no","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Roditi & Vafidis, 2019; \\\\uc0\\\\u220{}nal & Franquesa, 2010)","plainCitation":"(Roditi & Vafidis, 2019; Ünal & Franquesa, 2010)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31525,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/GGV8WY8D"],"itemData":{"id":31525,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Water (Switzerland)","DOI":"10.3390/w11071509","issue":"7","title":"Net fisheries'métiers in the eastern Mediterranean: Insights for small-scale fishery management on Kalymnos Island","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85073488463&doi=10.3390%2fw11071509&partnerID=40&md5=bbc1161f6aa598da67907a9f5690b540","volume":"11","author":[{"family":"Roditi","given":"K."},{"family":"Vafidis","given":"D."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31778,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/TSZKXD5N","http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/C5JF4X8Z"],"itemData":{"id":31778,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Journal of Applied Ichthyology","DOI":"10.1111/j.1439-0426.2009.01346.x","issue":"1","page":"26-34","title":"A comparative study on socio-economic indicators and viability in small-scale fisheries of six districts along the Turkish coast: Technical note","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-75649126862&doi=10.1111%2fj.1439-0426.2009.01346.x&partnerID=40&md5=fb4dea83d4a0dd9d8e6d6e5f9824a48e","volume":"26","author":[{"family":"Ünal","given":"V."},{"family":"Franquesa","given":"R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, but that these profits dropped consistently in recent decades ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"9OEtlQ39","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(F. Maynou, 2014; Pita, 2019b; Quetglas, 2016)","plainCitation":"(F. Maynou, 2014; Pita, 2019b; Quetglas, 2016)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":34075,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/I6SD7P3S"],"itemData":{"id":34075,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Journal of Applied Ichthyology","DOI":"10.1111/jai.12460","issue":"5","page":"978-985","title":"Bio-economic analysis of the Mar Menor (Murcia, SE Spain) small-scale lagoon fishery","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84908251441&doi=10.1111%2fjai.12460&partnerID=40&md5=de31f1e791a98aca1cd7ebfa70c485f8","volume":"30","author":[{"family":"Maynou","given":"F."},{"family":"Martínez-Baños","given":"P."},{"family":"Demestre","given":"M."},{"family":"Franquesa","given":"R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31787,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/4LT7EXU3"],"itemData":{"id":31787,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2018.09.018","page":"208-224","title":"Socioecological changes in data-poor S-fisheries: A hidden shellfisheries crisis in Galicia (NW Spain)","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85054149091&doi=10.1016%2fj.marpol.2018.09.018&partnerID=40&md5=bedbc67ea33abb4d2203c9dca2c8f17b","volume":"101","author":[{"family":"Pita","given":"P."},{"family":"Fernández-Márquez","given":"D."},{"family":"Antelo","given":"M."},{"family":"Macho","given":"G."},{"family":"Villasante","given":"S."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31791,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/5GBFQQID"],"itemData":{"id":31791,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Ocean and Coastal Management","DOI":"10.1016/j.ocecoaman.2016.09.013","page":"95-104","title":"Assessment and management of western Mediterranean small-scale fisheries","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84988974379&doi=10.1016%2fj.ocecoaman.2016.09.013&partnerID=40&md5=e332f25fed2740403e1e3d0d29fd30be","volume":"133","author":[{"family":"Quetglas","given":"A."},{"family":"Merino","given":"G."},{"family":"Ordines","given":"F."},{"family":"Guijarro","given":"B."},{"family":"Garau","given":"A."},{"family":"Grau","given":"A.M."},{"family":"Oliver","given":"P."},{"family":"Massutí","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. The reduction in market values and revenues is causing a marked change in local economies and in employment rates ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"6RR5HeXn","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(\\\\uc0\\\\u220{}nal & Franquesa, 2010)","plainCitation":"(Ünal & Franquesa, 2010)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31778,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/TSZKXD5N","http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/C5JF4X8Z"],"itemData":{"id":31778,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Journal of Applied Ichthyology","DOI":"10.1111/j.1439-0426.2009.01346.x","issue":"1","page":"26-34","title":"A comparative study on socio-economic indicators and viability in small-scale fisheries of six districts along the Turkish coast: Technical note","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-75649126862&doi=10.1111%2fj.1439-0426.2009.01346.x&partnerID=40&md5=fb4dea83d4a0dd9d8e6d6e5f9824a48e","volume":"26","author":[{"family":"Ünal","given":"V."},{"family":"Franquesa","given":"R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, with serious impacts on traditional fishing communities. It is estimated that the European small-scale fisheries dropped from 30-50% in terms of income over this time period ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a625el2kaq","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(J. Lloret, 2018)","plainCitation":"(J. Lloret, 2018)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":392,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/4LPJBJKI"],"itemData":{"id":392,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2016.11.007","page":"176-186","title":"Small-scale coastal fisheries in European Seas are not what they were: Ecological, social and economic changes","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85007195924&doi=10.1016%2fj.marpol.2016.11.007&partnerID=40&md5=7099a107b633d84556c70468ec43c71b","volume":"98","author":[{"family":"Lloret","given":"J."},{"family":"Cowx","given":"I.G."},{"family":"Cabral","given":"H."},{"family":"Castro","given":"M."},{"family":"Font","given":"T."},{"family":"Gonçalves","given":"J.M.S."},{"family":"Gordoa","given":"A."},{"family":"Hoefnagel","given":"E."},{"family":"Mati?-Skoko","given":"S."},{"family":"Mikkelsen","given":"E."},{"family":"Morales-Nin","given":"B."},{"family":"Moutopoulos","given":"D.K."},{"family":"Muñoz","given":"M."},{"family":"Santos","given":"M.N.","non-dropping-particle":"dos"},{"family":"Pintassilgo","given":"P."},{"family":"Pita","given":"C."},{"family":"Stergiou","given":"K.I."},{"family":"Ünal","given":"V."},{"family":"Veiga","given":"P."},{"family":"Erzini","given":"K."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. But in most of these cases small-scale fisheries continues as an important source of employment ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a100m95r3mv","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Baeta, 2018)","plainCitation":"(Baeta, 2018)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":370,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/YULEC7WK"],"itemData":{"id":370,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Ocean and Coastal Management","DOI":"10.1016/j.ocecoaman.2018.01.012","page":"143-154","title":"A socio-ecological approach to the declining Catalan clam fisheries","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85041434506&doi=10.1016%2fj.ocecoaman.2018.01.012&partnerID=40&md5=bb0511fa277fa86f86ceb212ad6d621a","volume":"154","author":[{"family":"Baeta","given":"M."},{"family":"Breton","given":"F."},{"family":"Ubach","given":"R."},{"family":"Ariza","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} even if fishers have to work additional jobs to maintain their livelihoods ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"H1WRpOZW","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Braga, 2019; F. Pereira, 2019)","plainCitation":"(Braga, 2019; F. Pereira, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31802,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/3GP2S3IU"],"itemData":{"id":31802,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Journal of Ethnobiology and Ethnomedicine","DOI":"10.1186/s13002-019-0345-9","issue":"1","title":"Ethnozoological knowledge of traditional fishing villages about the anadromous sea lamprey (Petromyzon marinus) in the Minho river, Portugal","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85077285236&doi=10.1186%2fs13002-019-0345-9&partnerID=40&md5=6dd7f95f450acf4eac9bd04130185fb5","volume":"15","author":[{"family":"Braga","given":"H.O."},{"family":"Pereira","given":"M.J."},{"family":"Morgado","given":"F."},{"family":"Soares","given":"A.M.V.M."},{"family":"Azeiteiro","given":"U.M."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31801,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/U39EH2JF"],"itemData":{"id":31801,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Research","DOI":"10.1016/j.fishres.2019.01.022","page":"117-125","title":"Catches of Sepia officinalis in the small-scale cuttlefish trap fishery off the Algarve coast (southern Portugal)","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85061696541&doi=10.1016%2fj.fishres.2019.01.022&partnerID=40&md5=eefd6a9ed819e68da369b3f5542e5000","volume":"214","author":[{"family":"Pereira","given":"F."},{"family":"Vasconcelos","given":"P."},{"family":"Moreno","given":"A."},{"family":"Gaspar","given":"M.B."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. The drop in profits, revenues and wages are not only due to overexploitation of stocks, the decrease in market values or to climate change. Competition is also increasing due to the introduction of industrial and recreational fishing, which have caused major reductions to commercial small-scale fisheries landings and profits ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"at795m7ojt","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Marengo, 2015; F. Maynou, 2013)","plainCitation":"(Marengo, 2015; F. Maynou, 2013)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31798,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/2BB3P5VE"],"itemData":{"id":31798,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Management and Ecology","DOI":"10.1111/fme.12110","issue":"3","page":"249-260","title":"Comparative analysis of artisanal and recreational fisheries for Dentex dentex in a Marine Protected Area","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84929265099&doi=10.1111%2ffme.12110&partnerID=40&md5=3d583f397f90edd8f42106c112c87d15","volume":"22","author":[{"family":"Marengo","given":"M."},{"family":"Culioli","given":"J.-M."},{"family":"Santoni","given":"M.-C."},{"family":"Marchand","given":"B."},{"family":"Durieux","given":"E.D.H."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}}},{"id":31788,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/FCXSQSHF"],"itemData":{"id":31788,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Research","DOI":"10.1016/j.fishres.2012.11.006","page":"11-17","title":"Small-scale fishery in the Balearic Islands (W Mediterranean): A socio-economic approach","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-8487117657