":"Zeller","given":"D."},{"family":"Harper","given":"S."},{"family":"Zylich","given":"K."},{"family":"Pauly","given":"D."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",2,28]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015",3]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Several countries appeared in only one or two studies; more studies addressed small-scale fisheries in Indonesia (18), the Philippines (10), Australia (7), India (9), Bangladesh (5) and the Solomon Islands (5). The overwhelming majority (82 %) of studies addressed coastal or marine and only 10 studies focused on inland small-scale fisheries, whereas three recent studies in Southeast Asia included both coastal and inland fisheries ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"Bwjgubfc","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Jahan, Ahsan, & Farque, 2017; Liao, 2019; Millar, 2019)","plainCitation":"(Jahan, Ahsan, & Farque, 2017; Liao, 2019; Millar, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31720,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/KT6V78SQ"],"itemData":{"id":31720,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Environment, Development and Sustainability","DOI":"10.1007/s10668-015-9740-0","issue":"2","page":"461-478","title":"Fishers’ local knowledge on impact of climate change and anthropogenic interferences on Hilsa fishery in South Asia: evidence from Bangladesh","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84949506409&doi=10.1007%2fs10668-015-9740-0&partnerID=40&md5=3805100345ebc784b4cd141a9c618a65","volume":"19","author":[{"family":"Jahan","given":"I."},{"family":"Ahsan","given":"D."},{"family":"Farque","given":"M.H."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}}},{"id":31719,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/DP478492"],"itemData":{"id":31719,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"ORYX","DOI":"10.1017/S003060531700117X","issue":"2","page":"222-229","title":"Wisdom of Crowds reveals decline of Asian horseshoe crabs in Beibu Gulf, China","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85033364817&doi=10.1017%2fS003060531700117X&partnerID=40&md5=31034b4b8486313e801d6b13cc3d27ae","volume":"53","author":[{"family":"Liao","given":"Y."},{"family":"Hsieh","given":"H.-L."},{"family":"Xu","given":"S."},{"family":"Zhong","given":"Q."},{"family":"Lei","given":"J."},{"family":"Liang","given":"M."},{"family":"Fang","given":"H."},{"family":"Xu","given":"L."},{"family":"Lin","given":"W."},{"family":"Xiao","given":"X."},{"family":"Chen","given":"C.-P."},{"family":"Cheung","given":"S.G."},{"family":"Kwan","given":"B.K.Y."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}},{"id":31815,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/JRFB5GSS"],"itemData":{"id":31815,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Environment, Development and Sustainability","DOI":"10.1007/s10668-018-0105-3","issue":"4","page":"1835-1852","title":"Local perceptions of changes in the use and management of floodplain fisheries commons: the case of Pak Peung wetland in Lao PDR","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85041908407&doi=10.1007%2fs10668-018-0105-3&partnerID=40&md5=028ca63770da18a18e028c1262fec095","volume":"21","author":[{"family":"Millar","given":"J."},{"family":"Robinson","given":"W."},{"family":"Baumgartner","given":"L."},{"family":"Homsombath","given":"K."},{"family":"Chittavong","given":"M."},{"family":"Phommavong","given":"T."},{"family":"Singhanouvong","given":"D."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Most studies report the uses of finfish, while fewer studies focus on other organisms (sharks, invertebrates). Several studies included many species (finfish and other organisms), evidencing the multi-species characteristic of these small-scale fisheries (see the data management report for Chapter 3 systematic literature review at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6452651).
	 Although some studies had short time series of up to one year, several studies analyzed time series of 10 years or more (see the data management report for Chapter 3 systematic literature review at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6452651) and at least one study included indigenous and local knowledge and archeological data to analyze a time series of 3,000 years in American Samoa ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"XoUDn6pa","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(P. Craig, Green, & Tuilagi, 2008)","plainCitation":"(P. Craig, Green, & Tuilagi, 2008)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1047,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/A875WIT3"],"itemData":{"id":1047,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Fisheries Research","DOI":"10.1016/j.fishres.2007.08.018","issue":"3","page":"230-240","title":"Subsistence harvest of coral reef resources in the outer islands of American Samoa: Modern, historic and prehistoric catches","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-39149126693&doi=10.1016%2fj.fishres.2007.08.018&partnerID=40&md5=3b51a3fc615d2c20af3fa5e686a4d167","volume":"89","author":[{"family":"Craig","given":"P."},{"family":"Green","given":"A."},{"family":"Tuilagi","given":"F."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2008"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Among the studies analyzing long time series of 50 to 60 years, some include indigenous and local knowledge on temporal trends ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a1cmk9oibtn","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Lavides, 2016; Muallil, Mamauag, Cababaro, Arceo, & Ali\\\\uc0\\\\u241{}o, 2014; Selgrath, Gergel, & Vincent, 2018a, 2018b; Thurstan, Buckley, Ortiz, & Pandolfi, 2016)","plainCitation":"(Lavides, 2016; Muallil, Mamauag, Cababaro, Arceo, & Aliño, 2014; Selgrath, Gergel, & Vincent, 2018a, 2018b; Thurstan, Buckley, Ortiz, & Pandolfi, 2016)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1065,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/7HUHCJDP