 D. Zeller, 2015)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1100,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/R5CQCPCK"],"itemData":{"id":1100,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Regional Studies in Marine Science","ISSN":"2352-4855","journalAbbreviation":"Regional Studies in Marine Science","page":"28-34","title":"Total marine fisheries catches in the Persian/Arabian Gulf from 1950 to 2010","volume":"2","author":[{"family":"Al-Abdulrazzak","given":"Dalal"},{"family":"Zeller","given":"Dirk"},{"family":"Belhabib","given":"Dyhia"},{"family":"Tesfamichael","given":"Dawit"},{"family":"Pauly","given":"Daniel"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":381,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/UU6WXXTT"],"itemData":{"id":381,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Frontiers in Marine Science","DOI":"10.3389/fmars.2017.00306","issue":"OCT","title":"An improved reconstruction of total marine fisheries catches for the New Hebrides and the Republic of Vanuatu, 1950-2014","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85032196916&doi=10.3389%2ffmars.2017.00306&partnerID=40&md5=724cce8c9475918b6ab610688a500812","volume":"4","author":[{"family":"Léopold","given":"M."},{"family":"David","given":"G."},{"family":"Raubani","given":"J."},{"family":"Kaltavara","given":"J."},{"family":"Hood","given":"L."},{"family":"Zeller","given":"D."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31756,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/7Z73PVY9"],"itemData":{"id":31756,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Coral Reefs","DOI":"10.1007/s00338-014-1219-1","ISSN":"0722-4028, 1432-0975","issue":"1","journalAbbreviation":"Coral Reefs","language":"en","page":"25-39","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Synthesis of underreported small-scale fisheries catch in Pacific island waters","URL":"http://link.springer.com/10.1007/s00338-014-1219-1","volume":"34","author":[{"family":"Zeller","given":"D."},{"family":"Harper","given":"S."},{"family":"Zylich","given":"K."},{"family":"Pauly","given":"D."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",2,28]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015",3]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}.
	Considerations or analyses related to economic sustainability were included in 45 and 11 of the reviewed studies on coastal and inland (or coastal and inland) small-scale fisheries, respectively (see the data management report for Chapter 3 systematic literature review at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6452651). Some of the ecologically sustainable or partially sustainable coastal fisheries also show net economic benefits due to improved or maintained catches, as observed for the shrimp fisheries in Indonesia ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"BNi7Ztog","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Anna, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Anna, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1048,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/P4HDFX28"],"itemData":{"id":1048,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Biodiversitas","DOI":"10.13057/biodiv/d180132","issue":"1","page":"248-256","title":"Indonesian shrimp resource accounting for sustainable stock management","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85007575346&doi=10.13057%2fbiodiv%2fd180132&partnerID=40&md5=40ae790b6fbb4d30fd250764e43122ae","volume":"18","author":[{"family":"Anna","given":"Z."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} and abalone fisheries in Australia ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"Nm3F8e8s","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Mayfield, Mundy, Gorfine, Hart, & Worthington, 2012)","plainCitation":"(Mayfield, Mundy, Gorfine, Hart, & Worthington, 2012)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":361,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/IKS7P457"],"itemData":{"id":361,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Reviews in Fisheries Science","DOI":"10.1080/10641262.2012.725434","issue":"4","page":"220-250","title":"Fifty years of sustained production from the Australian abalone fisheries","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84883494979&doi=10.1080%2f10641262.2012.725434&partnerID=40&md5=e454e226ff4869e559bf765e641c92b0","volume":"20","author":[{"family":"Mayfield","given":"S."},{"family":"Mundy","given":"C."},{"family":"Gorfine","given":"H."},{"family":"Hart","given":"A.M."},{"family":"Worthington","given":"D."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2012"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. 
	Fishing is an important economic activity for the Pacific Island countries located in the coral triangle area ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"kv7XYSjA","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Cruz-Trinidad, 2014)","plainCitation":"(Cruz-Trinidad, 2014)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1057,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/NQD2UQ88"],"itemData":{"id":1057,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Coastal Management","DOI":"10.1080/08920753.2014.877761","issue":"2","page":"160-182","title":"Linking Food Security with Coral Reefs and Fisheries in the Coral Triangle","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84893949295&doi=10.1080%2f08920753.2014.877761&partnerID=40&md5=6ebb7927d40611101d1b906904dc15ac","volume":"42","author":[{"family":"Cruz-Trinidad","given":"A."},{"family":"Aliño","given":"P.M."},{"family":"Geronimo","given":"R.C."},{"family":"Cabral","given":"R.B."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Some of the co-managed reef fisheries in Pacific Island countries can deliver tangible economic benefits to local communities in the form of increased catches ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"YEbo8p6L","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Tilley, Hunnam,, 2019; Webster, 2017; D. Yang & Pomeroy, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Tilley, Hunnam,, 2019; Webster, 2017; D. Yang & Pomeroy, 2017)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31731,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/7MYGCJQ8"],"itemData":{"id":31731,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Frontiers in Marine Science","DOI":"10.3389/fmars.2019.00392","issue":"JUL","title":"Evaluating the fit of co-management for small-scale fisheries governance in timor-leste","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85069781680&doi=10.3389%2ffmars.2019.00392&partnerID=40&md5=33e93601ea449dd2863fd1ce49cfa089","volume":"6","author":[{"family":"Tilley","given":"A."},{"family":"Hunnam","given":"K.J."},{"family":"Mills","given":"D.J."},{"family":"Steenbergen","given":"D.J."},{"family":"Govan","given":"H."},{"family":"Alonso-Poblacion","given":"E."},{"family":"Roscher","given":"M."},{"family":"Pereira","given":"M."},{"family":"Rodrigues","given":"P."},{"family":"Amador","given":"T."},{"family":"Duarte","given":"A."},{"family":"Gomes","given":"M."},{"family":"Cohen","given":"P.J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":357,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/69EEYSQU"],"itemData":{"id":357,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Research","DOI":"10.1016/j.fishres.2016.08.026","page":"168-176","title":"Detecting fisheries trends in a co-managed area in the Kingdom of Tonga","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84984675566&doi=10.1016%2fj.fishres.2016.08.026&partnerID=40&md5=dd3d3448a40c5b5329829689a6c5c647","volume":"186","author":[{"family":"Webster","given":"F.J."},{"family":"Cohen","given":"P.J."},{"family":"Malimali","given":"S."},{"family":"Tautai","given":"M."},{"family":"Vidler","given":"K."},{"family":"Mailau","given":"S."},{"family":"Vaipuna","given":"L."},{"family":"Fatongiatau","given":"V."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":360,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/QQW4K4VF"],"itemData":{"id":360,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2017.09.027","page":"173-181","title":"The impact of community-based fisheries management (CBFM) on equity and sustainability of small-scale coastal fisheries in the Philippines","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85032488364&doi=10.1016%2fj.marpol.2017.09.027&partnerID=40&md5=76d0c3c7aaacb7248e14d9e8598dda8d","volume":"86","author":[{"family":"Yang","given":"D."},{"family":"Pomeroy","given":"R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, for example, through periodic harvesting in protected areas, which can provide a needed boost to local economies ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"7uCROIT8","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(P. J. Cohen, Cinner, & Foale, 2013)","plainCitation":"(P. J. Cohen, Cinner, & Foale, 2013)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1051,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/RZETPG5C"],"itemData":{"id":1051,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Global Environmental Change","DOI":"10.1016/j.gloenvcha.2013.08.010","issue":"6","page":"1702-1713","title":"Fishing dynamics associated with periodically harvested marine closures","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84885425703&doi=10.1016%2fj.gloenvcha.2013.08.010&partnerID=40&md5=ef02c031492d506b97dbc6bc1ff869c6","volume":"23","author":[{"family":"Cohen","given":"P.J."},{"family":"Cinner","given":"J.E."},{"family":"Foale","given":"S."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. However, some highly valued economic resources, such as sea cucumbers or lobsters (Panulirus ornatus), have been overfished, particularly in the Philippines and Indonesia, due to increased market demands ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"9tDQUcV4","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Hair, Foale, Kinch, Yaman, & Southgate, 2016; Macusi, Laya-og, & Abreo, 2019; Prescott, Riwu, Prasetyo, & Stacey, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Hair, Foale, Kinch, Yaman, & Southgate, 2016; Macusi, Laya-og, & Abreo, 2019; Prescott, Riwu, Prasetyo, & Stacey, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31735,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/DRJLLXTX"],"itemData":{"id":31735,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Regional Studies in Marine Science","DOI":"10.1016/j.rsma.2016.02.001","page":"69-79","title":"Beyond boom, bust and ban: The sandfish (Holothuria scabra) fishery in the Tigak Islands, Papua New Guinea","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84958748927&doi=10.1016%2fj.rsma.2016.02.001&partnerID=40&md5=e116f18e258f57cafe4342028c36f58c","volume":"5","author":[{"family":"Hair","given":"C."},{"family":"Foale","given":"S."},{"family":"Kinch","given":"J."},{"family":"Yaman","given":"L."},{"family":"Southgate","given":"P.C."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31733,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/CSY2ZMI9"],"itemData":{"id":31733,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Ocean and Coastal Management","DOI":"10.1016/j.ocecoaman.2018.11.010","page":"340-349","title":"Wild lobster (Panulirus ornatus) fry fishery in Balete bay, Davao Oriental: Catch trends and implications to fisheries management","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85058150654&doi=10.1016%2fj.ocecoaman.2018.11.010&partnerID=40&md5=b153ada27a88e3a5b98d74a94710095f","volume":"168","author":[{"family":"Macusi","given":"E.D."},{"family":"Laya-og","given":"M.E."},{"family":"Abreo","given":"N.A.S."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31737,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/F54LKFKK"],"itemData":{"id":31737,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2017.03.033","page":"197-205","title":"The money side of livelihoods: Economics of an unregulated small-scale Indonesian sea cucumber fishery in the Timor Sea","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85017452886&doi=10.1016%2fj.marpol.2017.03.033&partnerID=40&md5=570c9d1e6fa2a6653d74f32bff10e791","volume":"82","author":[{"family":"Prescott","given":"J."},{"family":"Riwu","given":"J."},{"family":"Prasetyo","given":"A.P."},{"family":"Stacey","given":"N."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. The sea cucumbers fishery has high export value and provides an economic insurance for island populations of Pacific Island countries, but some of these fisheries had to be closed to recover, which compromised the economic benefits ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"wyGtJ5YE","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Eriksson, 2018; Hair, 2016)","plainCitation":"(Eriksson, 2018; Hair, 2016)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31738,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/8FU766DT"],"itemData":{"id":31738,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fish and Fisheries","DOI":"10.1111/faf.12255","issue":"2","page":"308-320","title":"Geography limits island small-scale fishery production","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85032841558&doi=10.1111%2ffaf.12255&partnerID=40&md5=de9686482b5c54c9b7d1cb955681b733","volume":"19","author":[{"family":"Eriksson","given":"H."},{"family":"Friedman","given":"K."},{"family":"Amos","given":"M."},{"family":"Bertram","given":"I."},{"family":"Pakoa","given":"K."},{"family":"Fisher","given":"R."},{"family":"Andrew","given":"N."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31735,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/DRJLLXTX"],"itemData":{"id":31735,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Regional Studies in Marine Science","DOI":"10.1016/j.rsma.2016.02.001","page":"69-79","title":"Beyond boom, bust and ban: The sandfish (Holothuria scabra) fishery in the Tigak Islands, Papua New Guinea","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84958748927&doi=10.1016%2fj.rsma.2016.02.001&partnerID=40&md5=e116f18e258f57cafe4342028c36f58c","volume":"5","author":[{"family":"Hair","given":"C."},{"family":"Foale","given":"S."},{"family":"Kinch","given":"J."},{"family":"Yaman","given":"L."},{"family":"Southgate","given":"P.C."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. 
	The economic sustainability of coastal fisheries could also be negatively affected by long market chains with strong inequalities in the distribution of profits between fishers and final retailers ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"QSmblRml","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(S.C.A. Ferse, Glaser, Neil, & Schwerdtner M\\\\uc0\\\\u225{}\\\\uc0\\\\u241{}ez, 2014)","plainCitation":"(S.C.A. Ferse, Glaser, Neil, & Schwerdtner Máñez, 2014)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":8795,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/S78WWUR9","http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/W6WNBIHG"],"itemData":{"id":8795,"type":"article-journal","abstract":"Small-scale fisheries in coral reef areas support the livelihoods of millions of people worldwide. Anthropogenic impacts such as overfishing and climate change increasingly threaten both the reef ecosystem and the livelihood security of the people that depend on the reefs. Adaptive management strategies are needed to adequately deal with these threats, but they require an understanding of the underlying drivers, which often originate and act on multiple levels. Using a social-ecological system approach, the coral reef fishery of the Spermonde Archipelago in South Sulawesi/Indonesia is assessed to identify key drivers and strategic leverage points for management. Under the influence of international markets and technological changes, several export-oriented fisheries have developed in the area that led to distinct subsequent peaks in fishing activity in a pattern of sequential marine resource exploitation. In response to stressors such as seasonality and overfishing of individual locations or species, a number of coping strategies have developed locally. These include extensive borrowing from fishing patrons, diversification of fishing methods, fishing migrations, and the crafting of local institutions to regulate fishing activity. However, the coping strategies hinder, and even decrease, the capacity of the system to adapt to future stressors and undermine the sustainability of the fishery. Potential strategies that target different levels of the fishery system in order to strengthen adaptive management are identified.","container-title":"Regional Environmental Change","DOI":"10.1007/s10113-012-0342-1","ISSN":"1436-378X","issue":"6","journalAbbreviation":"Reg Environ Change","language":"en","page":"2053-2065","source":"Springer Link","title":"To cope or to sustain? Eroding long-term sustainability in an Indonesian coral reef fishery","title-short":"To cope or to sustain?","URL":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10113-012-0342-1","volume":"14","author":[{"family":"Ferse","given":"Sebastian C. A."},{"family":"Glaser","given":"Marion"},{"family":"Neil","given":"Muhammad"},{"family":"Schwerdtner Máñez","given":"Kathleen"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2020",7,25]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014",12,1]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. The low price paid to fishers can interact with increased costs of fuel and other components of the fishing activity, prompting fishers to intensify their fishing effort to cover fishing trips to more distant fishing grounds ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"NZrX07lU","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Sebastian C. A. Ferse, Knittweis, Krause, Maddusila, & Glaser, 2012; G. M. N. Islam, Noh, Sidique, & Noh, 2014; Muallil, Mamauag, Cababaro,, 2014; Rhodes, Tupper, & Wichilmel, 2008)","plainCitation":"(Sebastian C. A. Ferse, Knittweis, Krause, Maddusila, & Glaser, 2012; G. M. N. Islam, Noh, Sidique, & Noh, 2014; Muallil, Mamauag, Cababaro,, 2014; Rhodes, Tupper, & Wichilmel, 2008)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1074,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/KAG8PLBI"],"itemData":{"id":1074,"type":"article-journal","abstract":"Collection of live coral for the marine aquarium trade has increased significantly in recent years, causing concerns over the ecological implications of this activity for the source regions. The Spermonde Archipelago off Southwest Sulawesi is one of the four major ornamental coral collection sites in Indonesia, the country supplying most corals in the trade. Management of the fishery remains ineffective, and overharvesting is widespread. Conservation strategies for marine resources increasingly emphasize the socioeconomic dimensions of resource use, yet little information is available on the livelihoods of fishermen involved in the ornamental fishery. Here, a first analysis of the livelihoods of coral fishermen in the Spermonde Archipelago is presented, along with a discussion of possibilities for future management interventions. The reef fishery of the study area is characterized by a high diversity of target organisms, with none of the fishermen relying exclusively on ornamental corals for income. Moreover, fishermen are organized in a tightly knit web of patron–client relationships, leaving little scope for them to initiate changes in livelihood strategies. The patron–client system emerged as a key institution of the fishery. In order to support sustainable marine resource use, management policies should simultaneously target the fishermen and their patrons as well as the regional coral trade network, broadening the livelihood portfolio of island communities and improving the regulation of the associated trade network.","container-title":"Coastal Management","DOI":"10.1080/08920753.2012.694801","ISSN":"0892-0753","issue":"5","note":"publisher: Taylor & Francis\\n_eprint: https://doi.org/10.1080/08920753.2012.694801","page":"525-555","source":"Taylor and Francis+NEJM","title":"Livelihoods of Ornamental Coral Fishermen in South Sulawesi/Indonesia: Implications for Management","title-short":"Livelihoods of Ornamental Coral Fishermen in South Sulawesi/Indonesia","URL":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08920753.2012.694801","volume":"40","author":[{"family":"Ferse","given":"Sebastian C. A."},{"family":"Knittweis","given":"Leyla"},{"family":"Krause","given":"Gesche"},{"family":"Maddusila","given":"Andi"},{"family":"Glaser","given":"Marion"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2020",10,27]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2012",9,1]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":1067,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/GMPPLL8Y"],"itemData":{"id":1067,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Research","DOI":"10.1016/j.fishres.2013.10.018","page":"122-129","title":"Economic impact of artificial reefs: A case study of small scale fishers in Terengganu, Peninsular Malaysia","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84893646100&doi=10.1016%2fj.fishres.2013.10.018&partnerID=40&md5=34da08bd4dc6168ce4af0326922ac51b","volume":"151","author":[{"family":"Islam","given":"G.M.N."},{"family":"Noh","given":"K.M."},{"family":"Sidique","given":"S.F."},{"family":"Noh","given":"A.F.M."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31718,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/QMLNCTQ3"],"itemData":{"id":31718,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2014.02.008","page":"110-117","title":"Catch trends in Philippine small-scale fisheries over the last five decades: The fishers perspectives","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84896754839&doi=10.1016%2fj.marpol.2014.02.008&partnerID=40&md5=bf977bf1b312e0bba9f84f16d3bc9fb0","volume":"47","author":[{"family":"Muallil","given":"R.N."},{"family":"Mamauag","given":"S.S."},{"family":"Cababaro","given":"J.T."},{"family":"Arceo","given":"H.O."},{"family":"Aliño","given":"P.M."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":1063,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/QBHMV6WH"],"itemData":{"id":1063,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Coral Reefs","DOI":"10.1007/s00338-007-0331-x","issue":"2","page":"443-454","title":"Characterization and management of the commercial sector of the Pohnpei coral reef fishery, Micronesia","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-42549094240&doi=10.1007%2fs00338-007-0331-x&partnerID=40&md5=1ec86efa3ed300b20f805f7df8cedfc3","volume":"27","author":[{"family":"Rhodes","given":"K.L."},{"family":"Tupper","given":"M.H."},{"family":"Wichilmel","given":"C.B."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2008"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}.
	Aspects related to the social and cultural sustainability were presented in 32 and 8 of the reviewed studies on coastal and inland small-scale fisheries, respectively (see the data management report for Chapter 3 systematic literature review at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6452651). Several studies highlighted the social benefits of these fisheries in the form of food provision and sustaining livelihoods of local communities ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"UmlFdaws","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Al-Abdulrazzak, 2015; Butler, Tawake, Skewes, Tawake, & McGrath, 2012; Cruz-Trinidad, 2014; Friedlander, 2014; Golden, Naisilsisili, Ligairi, & Drew, 2014; Rassweiler, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Al-Abdulrazzak, 2015; Butler, Tawake, Skewes, Tawake, & McGrath, 2012; Cruz-Trinidad, 2014; Friedlander, 2014; Golden, Naisilsisili, Ligairi, & Drew, 2014; Rassweiler, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1100,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/R5CQCPCK"],"itemData":{"id":1100,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Regional Studies in Marine Science","ISSN":"2352-4855","journalAbbreviation":"Regional Studies in Marine Science","page":"28-34","title":"Total marine fisheries catches in the Persian/Arabian Gulf from 1950 to 2010","volume":"2","author":[{"family":"Al-Abdulrazzak","given":"Dalal"},{"family":"Zeller","given":"Dirk"},{"family":"Belhabib","given":"Dyhia"},{"family":"Tesfamichael","given":"Dawit"},{"family":"Pauly","given":"Daniel"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":1046,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/5RQDTK8P"],"itemData":{"id":1046,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Ecology and Society","DOI":"10.5751/ES-05165-170434","issue":"4","title":"Integrating traditional ecological knowledge and fisheries management in the torres strait, Australia:The catalytic role of turtles and dugong as cultural keystone species","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84871997702&doi=10.5751%