one.0098036","issue":"5","title":"Combining natural history collections with fisher knowledge for community-based conservation in Fiji","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84901346358&doi=10.1371%2fjournal.pone.0098036&partnerID=40&md5=0d3f897736c63dea314fbae0abb9352c","volume":"9","author":[{"family":"Golden","given":"A.S."},{"family":"Naisilsisili","given":"W."},{"family":"Ligairi","given":"I."},{"family":"Drew","given":"J.A."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":1064,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/IK2I4JXB"],"itemData":{"id":1064,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Ambio","DOI":"10.1007/s13280-019-01154-5","issue":"1","page":"130-143","title":"Perceptions and responses of Pacific Island fishers to changing coral reefs","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85062647426&doi=10.1007%2fs13280-019-01154-5&partnerID=40&md5=99d42c652a32f18cf8c2a4018bb0a5f3","volume":"49","author":[{"family":"Rassweiler","given":"A."},{"family":"Lauer","given":"M."},{"family":"Lester","given":"S.E."},{"family":"Holbrook","given":"S.J."},{"family":"Schmitt","given":"R.J."},{"family":"Madi Moussa","given":"R."},{"family":"Munsterman","given":"K.S."},{"family":"Lenihan","given":"H.S."},{"family":"Brooks","given":"A.J."},{"family":"Wencélius","given":"J."},{"family":"Claudet","given":"J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Fishing is also an important cultural and social activity among many of the coastal fishing communities, reinforcing cultural identity and social practices, such as sharing fish, in the Pacific Island countries ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"Xw8lHAqN","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Golden, 2014; Rassweiler, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Golden, 2014; Rassweiler, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1068,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/PY77MAA8"],"itemData":{"id":1068,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"PLoS ONE","DOI":"10.1371/journal.pone.0098036","issue":"5","title":"Combining natural history collections with fisher knowledge for community-based conservation in Fiji","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84901346358&doi=10.1371%2fjournal.pone.0098036&partnerID=40&md5=0d3f897736c63dea314fbae0abb9352c","volume":"9","author":[{"family":"Golden","given":"A.S."},{"family":"Naisilsisili","given":"W."},{"family":"Ligairi","given":"I."},{"family":"Drew","given":"J.A."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":1064,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/IK2I4JXB"],"itemData":{"id":1064,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Ambio","DOI":"10.1007/s13280-019-01154-5","issue":"1","page":"130-143","title":"Perceptions and responses of Pacific Island fishers to changing coral reefs","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85062647426&doi=10.1007%2fs13280-019-01154-5&partnerID=40&md5=99d42c652a32f18cf8c2a4018bb0a5f3","volume":"49","author":[{"family":"Rassweiler","given":"A."},{"family":"Lauer","given":"M."},{"family":"Lester","given":"S.E."},{"family":"Holbrook","given":"S.J."},{"family":"Schmitt","given":"R.J."},{"family":"Madi Moussa","given":"R."},{"family":"Munsterman","given":"K.S."},{"family":"Lenihan","given":"H.S."},{"family":"Brooks","given":"A.J."},{"family":"Wencélius","given":"J."},{"family":"Claudet","given":"J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Indeed, Maori coastal fishers in New Zealand have perceived declines in culturally important nearshore resources (fish and invertebrates), which has negative cultural effects on communal activities, social connections, traditions, connections to nature and loss of pride of being able to feed themselves and guests by using seafood ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"Osl4HEtC","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Mccarthy, 2014)","plainCitation":"(Mccarthy, 2014)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1091,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/9LAW2SCD"],"itemData":{"id":1091,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Aquatic Conservation: Marine and Freshwater Ecosystems","DOI":"10.1002/aqc.2378","issue":"3","page":"369-390","title":"Local people see and care most? Severe depletion of inshore fisheries and its consequences for M?ori communities in New Zealand","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84901688900&doi=10.1002%2faqc.2378&partnerID=40&md5=bc82868394035d50398fa110105a11df","volume":"24","author":[{"family":"Mccarthy","given":"A."},{"family":"Hepburn","given":"C."},{"family":"Scott","given":"N."},{"family":"Schweikert","given":"K."},{"family":"Turner","given":"R."},{"family":"Moller","given":"H."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. 
	Besides improving catches and increasing the abundance of fishing resources, the commons-based management systems implemented in Pacific Islands can promote social sustainability through empowerment of local communities, increased compliance with management rules and the development of a sense of ownership of fishing resources ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"eUFjKd8G","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Butler, 2012; Cinner, 2012; Friedlander, 2014; Webster, 2017; D. Yang & Pomeroy, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Butler, 2012; Cinner, 2012; Friedlander, 2014; Webster, 2017; D. Yang & Pomeroy, 2017)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1046,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/5RQDTK8P"],"itemData":{"id":1046,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Ecology and Society","DOI":"10.5751/ES-05165-170434","issue":"4","title":"Integrating traditional ecological knowledge and fisheries management in the torres strait, Australia:The catalytic role of turtles and dugong as cultural keystone species","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84871997702&doi=10.5751%2fES-05165-170434&partnerID=40&md5=a3892b5090f7c5bfaf1e3fcd634545d1","volume":"17","author":[{"family":"Butler","given":"J.R.A."},{"family":"Tawake","given":"A."},{"family":"Skewes","given":"T."},{"family":"Tawake","given":"L."},{"family":"McGrath","given":"V."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2012"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31572,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/6NV2JEUT"],"itemData":{"id":31572,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences","DOI":"10.1073/pnas.1121215109","ISSN":"0027-8424, 1091-6490","issue":"14","journalAbbreviation":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences","language":"en","page":"5219-5222","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Comanagement of coral reef social-ecological systems","URL":"http://www.pnas.org/cgi/doi/10.1073/pnas.1121215109","volume":"109","author":[{"family":"Cinner"