"family":"Webster","given":"F.J."},{"family":"Cohen","given":"P.J."},{"family":"Malimali","given":"S."},{"family":"Tautai","given":"M."},{"family":"Vidler","given":"K."},{"family":"Mailau","given":"S."},{"family":"Vaipuna","given":"L."},{"family":"Fatongiatau","given":"V."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":360,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/QQW4K4VF"],"itemData":{"id":360,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2017.09.027","page":"173-181","title":"The impact of community-based fisheries management (CBFM) on equity and sustainability of small-scale coastal fisheries in the Philippines","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85032488364&doi=10.1016%2fj.marpol.2017.09.027&partnerID=40&md5=76d0c3c7aaacb7248e14d9e8598dda8d","volume":"86","author":[{"family":"Yang","given":"D."},{"family":"Pomeroy","given":"R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. These co-management systems often include community rules and beliefs, sometimes resulting in social benefits by participating communities even before perceived improvements on fisheries ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"B2hCXEcY","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Tilley, Hunnam,, 2019)","plainCitation":"(Tilley, Hunnam,, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31731,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/7MYGCJQ8"],"itemData":{"id":31731,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Frontiers in Marine Science","DOI":"10.3389/fmars.2019.00392","issue":"JUL","title":"Evaluating the fit of co-management for small-scale fisheries governance in timor-leste","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85069781680&doi=10.3389%2ffmars.2019.00392&partnerID=40&md5=33e93601ea449dd2863fd1ce49cfa089","volume":"6","author":[{"family":"Tilley","given":"A."},{"fam