iven":"E."},{"family":"Grau","given":"A.M."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31787,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/4LT7EXU3"],"itemData":{"id":31787,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2018.09.018","page":"208-224","title":"Socioecological changes in data-poor S-fisheries: A hidden shellfisheries crisis in Galicia (NW Spain)","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85054149091&doi=10.1016%2fj.marpol.2018.09.018&partnerID=40&md5=bedbc67ea33abb4d2203c9dca2c8f17b","volume":"101","author":[{"family":"Pita","given":"P."},{"family":"Fernández-Márquez","given":"D."},{"family":"Antelo","given":"M."},{"family":"Macho","given":"G."},{"family":"Villasante","given":"S."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":368,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/JXDXL3RN"],"itemData":{"id":368,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Frontiers in Marine Science","DOI":"10.3389/fmars.2017.00106","issue":"APR","title":"Harvest strategies for an ecosystem approach to fisheries management in western Mediterranean demersal fisheries","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85020168102&doi=10.3389%2ffmars.2017.00106&partnerID=40&md5=36df8f404ec7c77962f689a7da5e64d0","volume":"4","author":[{"family":"Quetglas","given":"A."},{"family":"Merino","given":"G."},{"family":"González","given":"J."},{"family":"Ordines","given":"F."},{"family":"Garau","given":"A."},{"family":"Grau","given":"A.M."},{"family":"Guijarro","given":"B."},{"family":"Oliver","given":"P."},{"family":"Massutí","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31781,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/83GSY46H"],"itemData":{"id":31781,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Ambio","DOI":"10.1007/s13280-015-0687-z","issue":"2","page":"230-240","title":"Assessing the sustainability and adaptive capacity of the gooseneck barnacle co-management system in Asturias, N. Spain","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84958103200&doi=10.1007%2fs13280-015-0687-z&partnerID=40&md5=f506dbfbd3232d883f84b2172d079bd5","volume":"45","author":[{"family":"Rivera","given":"A."},{"family":"Gelcich","given":"S."},{"family":"García-Flórez","given":"L."},{"family":"Acuña","given":"J.L."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":365,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/64CDWNTE"],"itemData":{"id":365,"type":"article-journal","abstract":"The Asturian gooseneck barnacle (Pollicipes pollicipes Gmelin, 1790) fishery has been managed through territorial use rights in fisheries (TURFs) since its inception >20 yrs ago. As part of this agreement, fishers are allotted exclusive extraction rights and active participation\\nin management strategies. In return for these rights, fishers are responsible for gathering data on effort and extraction in the fishery. We used the extensive time-series gathered by the fishers to assess the sustainability of the fishery. Additionally, we used survey techniques to explore\\nthe social-ecological drivers of this sustainability. The fishery has succeeded in maintaining or increasing catch per unit effort in all TURFs. Furthermore, the system has received public approval, where 73% of the stakeholders indicated that the only way to maintain a sustainable gooseneck\\nbarnacle fishery in Asturias is through the current management regime. The system has contributed to the sustainability of the fishery via: (1) creating a window of opportunity for management of the resource; (2) the continuous incorporation of scientific information and fishers' knowledge\\ninto management frameworks; (3) empowerment of the resource users; (4) embracing adaptive capacity through flexible management guidelines; and (5) matching management scales with the main life-history traits of the species. As in any dynamic system, the gooseneck barnacle fishery is currently\\nfaced with important challenges that might impact its sustainability, indicating that there are no simple recipes for fisheries management. Nonetheless, this system provides a set of basic principles for TURFs, which may be conducive to adaptive and sustainable fisheries.","container-title":"Bulletin of Marine Science","DOI":"10.5343/bms.2015.1080","issue":"1","journalAbbreviation":"Bulletin of Marine Science","page":"35-51","title":"Trends, drivers, and lessons from a long-term data series of the Asturian (northern Spain) gooseneck barnacle territorial use rights system","URL":"https://www.ingentaconnect.com/content/umrsmas/bullmar/2017/00000093/00000001/art00005","volume":"93","author":[{"family":"Rivera","given":"Antonella"},{"family":"Gelcich","given":"Stefan"},{"family":"García-Flórez","given":"Lucía"},{"family":"Acuña","given":"José Luis"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017",1,1]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31525,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/GGV8WY8D"],"itemData":{"id":31525,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Water (Switzerland)","DOI":"10.3390/w11071509","issue":"7","title":"Net fisheries'métiers in the eastern Mediterranean: Insights for small-scale fishery management on Kalymnos Island","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85073488463&doi=10.3390%2fw11071509&partnerID=40&md5=bbc1161f6aa598da67907a9f5690b540","volume":"11","author":[{"family":"Roditi","given":"K."},{"family":"Vafidis","given":"D."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31524,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/5988GD45"],"itemData":{"id":31524,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Management and Ecology","DOI":"10.1111/fme.12397","issue":"6","page":"661-673","title":"A selective and low impacting traditional fishery, sustaining the economy of small coastal villages in central Mediterranean: Keep or replace the small-scale driftnets?","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85074568061&doi=10.1111%2ffme.12397&partnerID=40&md5=aaa5f101e2bcccdd0f175c1aaf896c17","volume":"26","author":[{"family":"Sartor","given":"P."},{"family":"Carbonara","given":"P."},{"family":"Cerasi","given":"S."},{"family":"Lembo","given":"G."},{"family":"Facchini","given":"M.T."},{"family":"Lucchetti","given":"A."},{"family":"Sabatella","given":"R.F."},{"family":"Musumeci","given":"C."},{"family":"Zupa","given":"W."},{"family":"Spedicato","given":"M.T."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":34921,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/5TQXM7BB","http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/WASZNX6E"],"itemData":{"id":34921,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2018.03.027","language":"en","page":"268–275","title":"Ready for co-management? Portuguese artisanal octopus fishers’ preferences for management and knowledge about the resource","URL":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpol.2018.03.027","volume":"101","author":[{"family":"Silva","given":"P."},{"family":"Cabral","given":"H."},{"family":"Rangel","given":"M."},{"family":"Pereira","given":"J."},{"family":"Pita","given":"C."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31743,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/Z5GITNEQ"],"itemData":{"id":31743,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"ICES Journal of Marine Science","DOI":"10.1093/icesjms/fss161","issue":"1","page":"78-98","title":"A Métier-Sustainability-Index (MSI25) to evaluate fisheries components: Assessment of cases from data-poor fisheries from southern Europe","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84871241395&doi=10.1093%2ficesjms%2ffss161&partnerID=40&md5=935bf2d9dd994743163642d4ac3cd75c","volume":"70","author":[{"family":"Tzanatos","given":"E."},{"family":"Castro","given":"J."},{"family":"Forcada","given":"A."},{"family":"Mati?-Skoko","given":"S."},{"family":"Gaspar","given":"M."},{"family":"Koutsikopoulos","given":"C."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31779,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/RD855D5A"],"itemData":{"id":31779,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Mediterranean Marine Science","ISSN":"1791-6763","issue":"2","journalAbbreviation":"Mediterranean Marine Science","page":"309-342","title":"From bonito to anchovy: a reconstruction of Turkey’s marine fisheries catches (1950-2010)","volume":"14","author":[{"family":"Ulman","given":"A"},{"family":"Bekisoglu","given":"S"},{"family":"Zengin","given":"MA"},{"family":"Knudsen","given":"S"},{"family":"Unal","given":"VAHDET"},{"family":"Mathews","given":"C"},{"family":"Harper","given":"S"},{"family":"Zeller","given":"D"},{"family":"Pauly","given":"D"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}.
      Despite the fact that a very limited number of assessments based on the social perspective was found in the reviewed literature, these studies applied a diverse set of indicators. Those indicators were based on tradition (cultural, historic values) and on the level of dependence of the local communities on the fishing practices for their livelihoods ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"skPzwivP","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Guyader, 2013; \\\\uc0\\\\u220{}nal & Franquesa, 2010)","plainCitation":"(Guyader, 2013; Ünal & Franquesa, 2010)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31536,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/4DMSB5XK","http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/LDDKVXDP"],"itemData":{"id":31536,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Research","DOI":"10.1016/j.fishres.2012.11.008","page":"1-13","title":"Small scale fisheries in Europe: A comparative analysis based on a selection of case studies","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84872034772&doi=10.1016%2fj.fishres.2012.11.008&partnerID=40&md5=d5967ad8c05c9b3cbb471660793329b2","volume":"140","author":[{"family":"Guyader","given":"O."},{"family":"Berthou","given":"P."},{"family":"Koutsikopoulos","given":"C."},{"family":"Alban","given":"F."},{"family":"Demanèche","given":"S."},{"family":"Gaspar","given":"M.B."},{"family":"Eschbaum","given":"R."},{"family":"Fahy","given":"E."},{"family":"Tully","given":"O."},{"family":"Reynal","given":"L."},{"family":"Curtil","given":"O."},{"family":"Frangoudes","given":"K."},{"family":"Maynou","given":"F."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013"]]}}},{"id":31778,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/TSZKXD5N","http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/C5JF4X8Z"],"itemData":{"id":31778,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Journal of Applied Ichthyology","DOI":"10.1111/j.1439-0426.2009.01346.x","issue":"1","page":"26-34","title":"A comparative study on socio-economic indicators and viability in small-scale fisheries of six districts along the Turkish coast: Technical note","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-75649126862&doi=10.1111%2fj.1439-0426.2009.01346.x&partnerID=40&md5=fb4dea83d4a0dd9d8e6d6e5f9824a48e","volume":"26","author":[{"family":"Ünal","given":"V."},{"family":"Franquesa","given":"R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. The more frequent approach for social assessments was the use of the indicators of governance efficiency and effectiveness of fishers’ organizations in charge of co-management, or participatory management systems of aquatic resources ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"hADCafgn","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Baeta, 2018; Morales-Nin, 2017; P. Silva, 2019b)","plainCitation":"(Baeta, 2018; Morales-Nin, 2017; P. Silva, 2019b)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":370,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/YULEC7WK"],"itemData":{"id":370,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Ocean and Coastal Management","DOI":"10.1016/j.ocecoaman.2018.01.012","page":"143-154","title":"A socio-ecological approach to the declining Catalan clam fisheries","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85041434506&doi=10.1016%2fj.ocecoaman.2018.01.012&partnerID=40&md5=bb0511fa277fa86f86ceb212ad6d621a","volume":"154","author":[{"family":"Baeta","given":"M."},{"family":"Breton","given":"F."},{"family":"Ubach","given":"R."},{"family":"Ariza","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}}},{"id":369,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/Q3JJS23E"],"itemData":{"id":369,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"ICES Journal of Marine Science","DOI":"10.1093/icesjms/fsw227","issue":"7","page":"2053-2058","title":"Balearic Islands boat seine fisheries: The transparent goby fishery an example of co-management","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85021878888&doi=10.1093%2ficesjms%2ffsw227&partnerID=40&md5=be937c5449e3cbf68d4c133507f6d88c","volume":"74","author":[{"family":"Morales-Nin","given":"B."},{"family":"Grau","given":"A.M."},{"family":"Aguilar","given":"J.S."},{"family":"Del Mar Gil","given":"M."},{"family":"Pastor","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":34921,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/5TQXM7BB","http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/WASZNX6E"],"itemData":{"id":34921,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2018.03.027","language":"en","page":"268–275","title":"Ready for co-management? Portuguese artisanal octopus fishers’ preferences for management and knowledge about the resource","URL":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpol.2018.03.027","volume":"101","author":[{"family":"Silva","given":"P."},{"family":"Cabral","given":"H."},{"family":"Rangel","given":"M."},{"family":"Pereira","given":"J."},{"family":"Pita","given":"C."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. These may represent the main critical issues that are discussed by experts on the social perspectives of the European small-scale fishing and fishers.
      
* Africa
Since proper stock assessments are not very common (due to high costs, lack of personnel, time and other means) the authors used a diverse set of indicators. Only a small number of studies used stock assessments to produce estimates of maximum sustainable yield, yield per recruit, or cohort analysis and species-specific life table parameters ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"i4ikenFp","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Fulanda, 2011; Hara & Njaya, 2015; Jamu, 2011; Meissa, Gascuel, & Rivot, 2013; Rehren, Wolff, & Jiddawi, 2018)","plainCitation":"(Fulanda, 2011; Hara & Njaya, 2015; Jamu, 2011; Meissa, Gascuel, & Rivot, 2013; Rehren, Wolff, & Jiddawi, 2018)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31806,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/TETVNFUT"],"itemData":{"id":31806,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Ocean and Coastal Management","DOI":"10.1016/j.ocecoaman.2010.12.010","issue":"5","page":"401-414","title":"Fishery trends, resource-use and management system in the Ungwana Bay fishery Kenya","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-79953278271&doi=10.1016%2fj.ocecoaman.2010.12.010&partnerID=40&md5=47e5e9ee2ee1c96c29e5a17763018c09","volume":"54","author":[{"family":"Fulanda","given":"B."},{"family":"Ohtomi","given":"J."},{"family":"Mueni","given":"E."},{"family":"Kimani","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2011"]]}}},{"id":31748,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/IDA5KDZE"],"itemData":{"id":31748,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Research","DOI":"10.1016/j.fishres.2015.08.005","page":"10-18","title":"Between a rock and a hard place: The need for and challenges to implementation of Rights Based Fisheries Management in small-scale fisheries of southern Lake Malawi","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84940492487&doi=10.1016%2fj.fishres.2015.08.005&partnerID=40&md5=cd9365c18cb7f0cf2ff30eaec22047c8","volume":"174","author":[{"family":"Hara","given":"M."},{"family":"Njaya","given":"F."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31528,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/9LAI5MQ5"],"itemData":{"id":31528,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Journal of Great Lakes Research","DOI":"10.1016/j.jglr.2010.11.017","issue":"SUPPL. 1","page":"3-14","title":"Challenges to sustainable management of the lakes of Malawi","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-79952695965&doi=10.1016%2fj.jglr.2010.11.017&partnerID=40&md5=13fdc8fe7d639007c33e2f09e241cb28","volume":"37","author":[{"family":"Jamu","given":"D."},{"family":"Banda","given":"M."},{"family":"Njaya","given":"F."},{"family":"Hecky","given":"R.E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2011"]]}}},{"id":1061,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/XZYGQEB8"],"itemData":{"id":1061,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"African Journal of Marine Science","DOI":"10.2989/1814232X.2013.798244","issue":"2","page":"253-267","title":"Assessing stocks in data-poor African fisheries: a case study on the white grouper Epinephelus aeneus of Mauritania","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84882245182&doi=10.2989%2f1814232X.2013.798244&partnerID=40&md5=1d04f88e950f1ac44ffd4c4ea38b7746","volume":"35","author":[{"family":"Meissa","given":"B."},{"family":"Gascuel","given":"D."},{"family":"Rivot","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31750,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/63XI6UZP"],"itemData":{"id":31750,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Journal of Applied Ichthyology","DOI":"10.1111/jai.13578","issue":"1","page":"117-128","title":"Fisheries assessment of Chwaka Bay (Zanzibar) – following a holistic approach","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85040720923&doi=10.1111%2fjai.13578&partnerID=40&md5=c3eaaad4eeeffe153bace5399755d1eb","volume":"34","author":[{"family":"Rehren","given":"J."},{"family":"Wolff","given":"M."},{"family":"Jiddawi","given":"N."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Most of the assessments support their conclusions based on series of catch/production, such as landing statistics. Catch biomass (biomass landed) and catch composition (species landed) are the more frequent parameters in the ecological evaluations. Nevertheless, catch-per-unit-of-effort and size distribution of fish landed are also frequently used indicators. More than 45 papers use fish landings and/or catch-per-unit-of-effort as indicators to support their analysis (see the data management report for Chapter 3 systematic literature review at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6452651). 
      Additional indicators were used for the assessment of economic and social aspects. Indicators for economic evaluation were revenue and market prices ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"ZH3hhOjb","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Blythe, Murray, & Flaherty, 2013)","plainCitation":"(Blythe, Murray, & Flaherty, 2013)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31723,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/FLD53N28"],"itemData":{"id":31723,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Ecology and Society","DOI":"10.5751/ES-05759-180465","issue":"4","title":"Historical perspectives and recent trends in the coastal Mozambican fishery","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84891877244&doi=10.5751%2fES-05759-180465&partnerID=40&md5=227a49b5dfdea88be2cb900a54d26d8f","volume":"18","author":[{"family":"Blythe","given":"J.L."},{"family":"Murray","given":"G."},{"family":"Flaherty","given":"M.S."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, relevance of foreign markets for exportations, and added costs and values ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"QEKKT5mc","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Baker-M\\\\uc0\\\\u233{}dard & Faber, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Baker-Médard & Faber, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1054,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/DLZT9JJK"],"itemData":{"id":1054,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Marine Policy","DOI":"10.1016/j.marpol.2019.103805","title":"Fins and (Mis)fortunes: Managing shark populations for sustainability and food sovereignty","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85077659355&doi=10.1016%2fj.marpol.2019.103805&partnerID=40&md5=7e9e9628c5a4b3f51b0e5437ea47478a","volume":"113","author":[{"family":"Baker-Médard","given":"M."},{"family":"Faber","given":"J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/mast