* Latin America
This review evidenced the limitations imposed by the lack of continuous monitoring to provide fisheries and biological data to evaluate sustainable use. Only a few studies included more detailed population analyses and measured conventional stock parameters, such as maximum sustainable yield, natural mortality, fishing mortality, among others ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"HuYyjHlq","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Aburto & Stotz, 2013; Baig\\\\uc0\\\\u250{}n, Minotti, & Oldani, 2013; M. F. Catarino, Kahn, & Freitas, 2019; Cavieses N\\\\uc0\\\\u250{}\\\\uc0\\\\u241{}ez, Ojeda Ruiz De La Pen\\\\uc0\\\\u227{}, Flores Irigollen, Rodr\\\\uc0\\\\u237{}guez Rodr\\\\uc0\\\\u237{}guez, & Jardim, 2018; Duarte, 2018; Mart\\\\uc0\\\\u237{}nez-Candelas, 2020; Mesquita, Cruz, Hallwass, & Isaac, 2019)","plainCitation":"(Aburto & Stotz, 2013; Baigún, Minotti, & Oldani, 2013; M. F. Catarino, Kahn, & Freitas, 2019; Cavieses Núñez, Ojeda Ruiz De La Penã, Flores Irigollen, Rodríguez Rodríguez, & Jardim, 2018; Duarte, 2018; Martínez-Candelas, 2020; Mesquita, Cruz, Hallwass, & Isaac, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":390,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/8ZMQRYKF"],"itemData":{"id":390,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Ocean and Coastal Management","DOI":"10.1016/j.ocecoaman.2012.10.013","page":"88-98","title":"Learning about TURFs and natural variability: Failure of surf clam management in Chile","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84869869570&doi=10.1016%2fj.ocecoaman.2012.10.013&partnerID=40&md5=4aebaba544b49db1ea191ef249232eda","volume":"71","author":[{"family":"Aburto","given":"J."},{"family":"Stotz","given":"W."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31724,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/MD6C8WUE"],"itemData":{"id":31724,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Neotropical Ichthyology","DOI":"10.1590/S1679-62252013000100023","issue":"1","page":"199-210","title":"Assessment of sáb