mple, year of the best catch) or as an interval categorical variable (for example, discrete years or decades according to fishers’ age groups, specific events, etc.) (Table 3.3.). 
	Most of the studies reported declining trends in abundance, catch-per-unit-of-effort or size of fishing resources (Table 3.3). Reported declines were usually focused on threatened species, some of which had been intensely exploited, such as reef fishes from the genus Epinephelus and Mycteroperca (groupers) ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a21rfoemjti","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Bender, Floeter, & Hanazaki, 2013; Bender, 2014; Bunce, Rodwell, Gibb, & Mee, 2008; Castellanos-Galindo, 2018; Giglio, 2015; Ribeiro, Damasio, & Silvano, 2021a; C. Zapelini, Bender, Giglio, & Schiavetti, 2019a)","plainCitation":"(Bender, Floeter, & Hanazaki, 2013; Bender, 2014; Bunce, Rodwell, Gibb, & Mee, 2008; Castellanos-Galindo, 2018; Giglio, 2015; Ribeiro, Damasio, & Silvano, 2021a; C. Zapelini, Bender, Giglio, & Schiavetti, 2019a)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":1070,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/7QPDZQJE"],"itemData":{"id":1070,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Fisheries Management and Ecology","DOI":"10.1111/fme.12006","issue":"1","page":"58-67","title":"Do traditional fishers recognise reef fish species declines? Shifting environmental baselines in Eastern Brazil","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84872554669&doi=10.1111%2ffme.12006&partnerID=40&md5=0bd0067395f01905acbcff8ba284b983","volume":"20","author":[{"family":"Bender","given":"M.G."},{"family":"Floeter","given":"S.R."},{"family":"Hanazaki","given":"N."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":1069,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/N38WH2T5"],"itemData":{"id":1069,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"PLoS ONE","DOI":"10.1371/journal.pone.0110332","issue":"10","title":"Local ecological knowledge and scientific data reveal overexploitation by multigear artisanal fisheries in the Southwestern Atlantic","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84908036980&doi=10.1371%2fjournal.pone.011033