	A phenomenon sometimes related to studies based on fishers’ memories to reconstruct past events is known as shifting baseline syndrome, i.e., environmental changes may be recognized only by older fishers and underestimated or not recognized by younger ones ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"DYVp05dU","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Papworth, Rist, Coad, & Milner-Gulland, 2009; Daniel Pauly, 1995)","plainCitation":"(Papworth, Rist, Coad, & Milner-Gulland, 2009; Daniel Pauly, 1995)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31755,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/V6FSTJV3"],"itemData":{"id":31755,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Conservation Letters","DOI":"10.1111/j.1755-263X.2009.00049.x","ISSN":"1755263X, 1755263X","language":"en","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Evidence for shifting baseline syndrome in conservation","URL":"http://doi.wiley.com/10.1111/j.1755-263X.2009.00049.x","author":[{"family":"Papworth","given":"S.K."},{"family":"Rist","given":"J."},{"family":"Coad","given":"L."},{"family":"Milner-Gulland","given":"E.J."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2020",5,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2009",1]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31771,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/Q3R795NU"],"itemData":{"id":31771,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Trends in ecology & evolution","ISSN":"0169-5347","issue":"10","journalAbbreviation":"Trends in ecology & evolution","page":"430","title":"Anecdotes and the shifting baseline syndrome of fisheries","volume":"10","author":[{"family":"Pauly","given":"Daniel"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["1995"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Shifting baseline has been observed by many studies worldwide, which reported an influence of age on fishers’ perceptions about changes in the abundance of fisheries resources ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"anqj66gkou","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Bender, 20