/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, cod ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"EbCQ0rkI","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Dinesen, 2019a)","plainCitation":"(Dinesen, 2019a)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31530,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/ED7EN3JG"],"itemData":{"id":31530,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Journal of Coastal Conservation","DOI":"10.1007/s11852-019-00711-0","issue":"5","page":"943-958","title":"Cod and climate: a systems approach for sustainable fisheries management of Atlantic cod (Gadus morhua) in coastal Danish waters","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85073975119&doi=10.1007%2fs11852-019-00711-0&partnerID=40&md5=0a852f0fec2b71c72780a25d5feecfb7","volume":"23","author":[{"family":"Dinesen","given":"G.E."},{"family":"Neuenfeldt","given":"S."},{"family":"Kokkalis","given":"A."},{"family":"Lehmann","given":"A."},{"family":"Egekvist","given":"J."},{"family":"Kristensen","given":"K."},{"family":"Munk","given":"P."},{"family":"Hüssy","given":"K."},{"family":"Støttrup","given":"J.G."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, anchovies and sardines ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"8DMRxpKZ","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Sartor, 2019)","plainCitation":"(Sartor, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31524,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/5988GD45"],"itemData":{"id":31524,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Management and Ecology","DOI":"10.1111/fme.12397","issue":"6","page":"661-673","title":"A selective and low impacting traditional fishery, sustaining the economy of small coastal villages in central Mediterranean: Keep or replace the small-scale driftnets?","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85074568061&doi=10.1111%2ffme.12397&partnerID=40&md5=aaa5f101e2bcccdd0f175c1aaf896c17","volume":"26","author":[{"family":"Sartor","given":"P."},{"family":"Carbonara","given":"P."},{"family":"Cerasi","given":"S."},{"family":"Lembo","given":"G."},{"family":"Facchini","given":"M.T."},{"family":"Lucchetti","given":"A."},{"family":"Sabatella","given":"R.F."},{"family":"Musumeci","given":"C."},{"family":"Zupa","given":"W."},{"family":"Spedicato","given":"M.T."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}.  
      As indicated by 47 out of the 63 papers reviewed, small-scale fisheries systems are often unsustainable, although varying levels of sustainability were observed in 30% of the papers (see the data management report for Chapter 3 systematic literature review at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6452651). This applies equally to inland, coastal and marine/oceanic fishing. A number of studies described multi-faceted fishing systems, where some stocks were sustainably exploited while others were not. In 74% of the papers, focusing on broader analysis, and using long and consistent series of data (a set comprising 19 papers), unsustainability elements were still observed. 
	Approximately 10% of the reviewed papers report cases of partial sustainability and 16% report sustainable cases of small-scale fishing (see the data management report for Chapter 3 systematic literature review at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6452651). The cases of sustainable fishing reported are mainly supported by enabling factors that reflect the adoption of sound management decisions and measures. These are systems that successfully controlled the fishing effort ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"aoasq9igmv","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Fourt, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Fourt, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31807,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/E4MG39TK"],"itemData":{"id":31807,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Regional Environmental Change","DOI":"10.1007/s10113-020-01581-1","issue":"1","title":"Past and present of a Mediterranean small-scale fishery: the Greek sponge fishery—its resilience and sustainability","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85078476313&doi=10.1007%2fs10113-020-01581-1&partnerID=40&md5=3093b42cd59d219ab6e4b9d61cd168ee","volume":"20","author":[{"family":"Fourt","given":"M."},{"family":"Faget","given":"D."},{"family":"Dailianis","given":"T."},{"family":"Koutsoubas","given":"D."},{"family":"Pérez","given":"T."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, and enforced the regulation of zones of use and no-use (no-take), determined by officially protected marine areas or estuaries ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"aehcdogo6c","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(C. Antunes, 2015; Guidetti & Claudet, 2010; Marengo, 2015; Morales-Nin, 2017)","plainCitation":"(C. Antunes, 2015; Guidetti & Claudet, 2010; Marengo, 2015; Morales-Nin, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31782,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/C4RFSYFY"],"itemData":{"id":31782,"type":"chapter","container-title":"Freshwater Fisheries Ecology","event-place":"Oxford, UK","ISBN":"978-1-118-39442-7","note":"DOI: 10.1002/9781118394380.ch23","page":"268-282","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","publisher-place":"Oxford, UK","title":"Iberian inland fisheries","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84984844857&doi=10.1002%2f9781118394380.ch23&partnerID=40&md5=c6a7af8f3dd1d871e5423260a9b0aae9","author":[{"family":"Antunes","given":"C."},{"family":"Cobo","given":"F."},{"family":"Araújo","given":"M.J."}],"editor":[{"family":"Craig","given":"J.F."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}}},{"id":31894,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/72ZHAWD6"],"itemData":{"id":31894,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Conservation Biology","ISSN":"0888-8892","issue":"1","journalAbbreviation":"Conservation Biology","page":"312-318","title":"Comanagement practices enhance fisheries in marine protected areas","volume":"24","author":[{"family":"Guidetti","given":"Paolo"},{"family":"Claudet","given":"Joachim"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010"]]}},"label":"page"},{"id":31798,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/2BB3P5VE"],"itemData":{"id":31798,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"Fisheries Management and Ecology","DOI":"10.1111/fme.12110","issue":"3","page":"249-260","title":"Comparative analysis of artisanal and recreational fisheries for Dentex dentex in a Marine Protected Area","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84929265099&doi=10.1111%2ffme.12110&partnerID=40&md5=3d583f397f90edd8f42106c112c87d15","volume":"22","author":[{"family":"Marengo","given":"M."},{"family":"Culioli","given":"J.-M."},{"family":"Santoni","given":"M.-C."},{"family":"Marchand","given":"B."},{"family":"Durieux","given":"E.D.H."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}}},{"id":369,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/Q3JJS23E"],"itemData":{"id":369,"type":"article-journal","archive":"Scopus","container-title":"ICES Journal of Marine Science","DOI":"10.1093/icesjms/fsw227","issue":"7","page":"2053-2058","title":"Balearic Islands boat seine fisheries: The transparent goby fishery an example of co-management","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85021878888&doi=10.1093%2ficesjms%2ffsw227&partnerID=40&md5=be937c5449e3cbf68d4c133507f6d88c","volume":"74","author":[{"family":"Morales-Nin","given":"B."},{"family":"Grau","given":"A.M."},{"family":"Aguilar","given":"J.S."},{"family":"Del Mar Gil","given":"M."},{"family":"Pastor","given":"E."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"label":"page"}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. 
	The reported cases of unsustainability of small-scale fishing for food and feed are due to a larger and more diverse array of inter-related causes. Fishing pressure above the capacity of the stocks was mentioned by 41% of the papers. This leads to overfishing (either of the targeted species or of their prey species), catches above the maximum sustainable yield, or to the reduction in catch-per-unit-of-effort ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a1ajjtghujj","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(E. Azzurro, 2019; Corral & Manrique de Lara, 2017; Duncan, 2016; Figus, 2017; J. Lloret, 2018; Quetglas, 2016)","plainCitation":"(E. Azzurro, 2019; Corral & Manrique de Lara, 2017; Duncan, 2016; Figus, 2017; J. Lloret, 2018; Quetglas, 2016)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31523,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/74B9LVWF"],"itemData":{"id":31523,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Global Change Biology","DOI":"10.1111/gcb.14670","issue":"8","page":"2779-2792","title":"Climate change, biological invasions, and the shifting distribution of Mediterranean fishes: A large-scale survey based on local ecological knowledge","URL":"https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85066148934&doi=10.1111%2fgcb.14670&partnerID=40&md5=95b99b21ed80310b03870fadec887f45","volume":"25","author":[{"family":"Azzurro","given":"E."},{"family":"Sbragaglia","given":"V."},{"family":"Cerri","given":"J."},{"family":"Bariche","given":"M."},{"family":"Bolognini","given":"L."},{"family":"Ben Souissi","given":"J."},{"family":"Busoni","given":"G."},{"family":"Coco","given":"S."},{"family":"Chryssanthi","given":"A."},{"family":"Fanelli","given":"E."},{"family":"Ghanem","given":"R."},{"family":"Garrabou","given":"J."},{"family":"Gianni","given":"F."},{"family":"Grati","given":"F."},{"family":"Kolitari","given":"J."},{"family":"Guglielmo","given":"L."},{"family":"Lipej","given":"L."},{"family":"Mazzoldi","given":"C."},{"family":"Milone","given":"N."},{"family":"Pan