      Removing the bark may threaten the survival of plant individual, for example when gathering the medicinal part of the African cherry (Prunus africana) ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a1231o7lq72","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Fashing, 2004; K. M. Stewart, 2003)","plainCitation":"(Fashing, 2004; K. M. Stewart, 2003)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30730,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/BWQ25FE7"],"itemData":{"id":30730,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Biological Conservation","DOI":"10.1016/j.biocon.2004.03.018","ISSN":"0006-3207","issue":"4","page":"449-459","title":"Mortality trends in the African cherry (Prunus africana) and the implications for colobus monkeys (Colobus guereza) in Kakamega Forest, Kenya","volume":"120","author":[{"family":"Fashing","given":"Peter J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2004"]]}}},{"id":33462,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/UCD2984J"],"itemData":{"id":33462,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Journal of Ethnopharmacology","DOI":"10.1016/j.jep.2003.08.002","ISSN":"0378-8741","issue":"1","page":"3-13","title":"The African cherry (Prunus africana): Can lessons be learned from an over-exploited medicinal tree?","volume":"89","author":[{"family":"Stewart","given":"K. M."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2003"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, Julbernardia paniculata, Isoberlinia angolensis ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a252dr3t5l4","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Chungu, Muimba-Kankolongo, Roux, & Malambo, 2007)","plainCitation":"(Chungu, Muimba-Kankolongo, Roux, & Malambo, 2007)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30997,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/CCD435TF"],"itemData":{"id":30997,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Southern Hemisphere Forestry Journal","DOI":"10.2989/SHFJ.2007.69.3.4.354","ISSN":"1991-931X","issue":"3","page":"157-163","title":"Bark removal for medicinal use pr