3.3.2.2. The diversity of contemporary gathering

3.3.2.2.1. Gathering in Western European and Other Group (WEOG) Countries

Gathering wild algae, fungi and plants is often assumed to be an activity more prevalent in developing countries and the Global South, and less so in post-industrial countries. However, results of surveys conducted in Europe, North America, and the United Kingdom over the last 20 years suggest high rates of participation in gathering by individuals and households in many of the countries in these regions (Table 3.7). In Scotland, a 2003 random sample general population survey found 18% of individuals had gathered fungi and tree or plant-derived materials in the previous 12 months, including residents of both urban and rural areas ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"R1neroUP","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(M. Emery, 2006)","plainCitation":"(M. Emery, 2006)","dontUpdate":true,"noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":982,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/DQ5PEQ2U"],"itemData":{"id":982,"type":"report","event-place":"Edinburgh","genre":"government report","language":"English","page":"i-viii + 1-40","publisher":"Forestry Commission","publisher-place":"Edinburgh","title":"Wild harvests from Scottish Woodlands: social, cultural, and economic values of contemporary non-timber forest products","author":[{"family":"Emery","given":"Marla"},{"family":"Martin","given":"Suzanne"},{"family":"Dyke","given":"Alison"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2006"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. The Northeastern United States of America includes both the largest urban concentrations of that nation and substantial rural lands. Eighteen percent of respondents to a 2004 survey in that subnational region reported that they had gathered “tree or plant materials around woodlands: e.g., mushrooms, berries, cones, or moss” in the previous 12 months, while 26% had done so in the previous 5 years. Also in the Northeastern United States of America, 36% of respondents to a survey conducted over the five-year period 2005-2009 indicated they had picked mushrooms and/or berries in the previous 12 months ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a160j8l8des","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Cordell, Betz, Mou, & Gormanson, 2012; K. Watson, 2018)","plainCitation":"(Cordell, Betz, Mou, & Gormanson, 2012; K. Watson, 2018)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":33294,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/W4LHZQQF"],"itemData":{"id":33294,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"In: Chamberlain, James L.; Emery, Marla R.; Patel-Weynand, Toral, eds. 2018. Assessment of nontimber forest products in the United States under changing conditions. Gen. Tech. Rep. SRS–232. Asheville, NC: U.S. Department of Agriculture, Forest Service, Southern Research Station","language":"en","page":"102-117","source":"www.fs.usda.gov","title":"Social dimensions of nontimber forest products","URL":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/treesearch/pubs/57299","volume":"2018","author":[{"family":"Watson","given":"Kelly"},{"family":"Christian","given":"Colmore S."},{"family":"Emery","given":"Marla R."},{"family":"Hurley","given":"Patrick T."},{"family":"McLain","given":"Rebecca J."},{"family":"Wilmsen","given":"Carl"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",3,29]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}}},{"id":965,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/JKZYQ3CJ"],"itemData":{"id":965,"type":"report","event-place":"Newtown Square, PA","language":"en","note":"DOI: 10.2737/NRS-GTR-100","number":"NRS-GTR-100","page":"NRS-GTR-100","publisher":"U.S. Department of Agriculture, Forest Service, Northern Research Station","publisher-place":"Newtown Square, PA","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Outdoor Recreation in the Northern United States","URL":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/treesearch/pubs/41528","author":[{"family":"Cordell","given":"H. Ken"},{"family":"Betz","given":"Carter J."},{"family":"Mou","given":"Shela H."},{"family":"Gormanson","given":"Dale D."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",3,29]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2012"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. A 2016 survey of households in 28 European countries found that Europe-wide, 26% of households had gathered in the previous 12 months, ranging from 4% of households in the Netherlands to 68% of households in Latvia ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a176pgjbaqv","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(B. Wolfslehner, Prokofieva, & Mavsar, 2019)","plainCitation":"(B. Wolfslehner, Prokofieva, & Mavsar, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30991,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/IVV5KSPW"],"itemData":{"id":30991,"type":"report","publisher":"European  Forest Institute","title":"Non-wood forest products in Europe: Seeing the forest  around the trees. What Science Can Tell Us 10.","URL":"https://efi.int/sites/default/files/files/publication-bank/2019/efi_wsctu_10_2019.pdf","author":[{"family":"Wolfslehner","given":"B."},{"family":"Prokofieva","given":"I."},{"family":"Mavsar","given":"R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. This study noted a general pattern of highest rates of gathering by households in Eastern Europe ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"aih5pcvvva","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Lovri\\\\uc0\\\\u263{}, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Lovri?, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":985,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/HWFFDQ7B"],"itemData":{"id":985,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Forest Policy and Economics","DOI":"10.1016/j.forpol.2020.102175","ISSN":"13899341","journalAbbreviation":"Forest Policy and Economics","language":"en","page":"102175","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Non-wood forest products in Europe – A quantitative overview","URL":"https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S1389934120300654","volume":"116","author":[{"family":"Lovri?","given":"Marko"},{"family":"Da Re","given":"Riccardo"},{"family":"Vidale","given":"Enrico"},{"family":"Prokofieva","given":"Irina"},{"family":"Wong","given":"Jennifer"},{"family":"Pettenella","given":"Davide"},{"family":"Verkerk","given":"Pieter Johannes"},{"family":"Mavsar","given":"Robert"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",3,29]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020",7]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Unlike the surveys in Scotland and the United States of America, the European study documented gathering by households, suggesting that the percentage of individuals gathering in the region may be higher.

