 2572-2611","issue":"5","journalAbbreviation":"Plants People Planet","language":"en","page":"515-534","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"International collaboration between collections?based institutes for halting biodiversity loss and unlocking the useful properties of plants and fungi","URL":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ppp3.10149","volume":"2","author":[{"family":"Pearce","given":"Timothy R."},{"family":"Antonelli","given":"Alexandre"},{"family":"Brearley","given":"Francis Q."},{"family":"Couch","given":"Charlotte"},{"family":"Campostrini Forzza","given":"Rafaela"},{"family":"Gonçalves","given":"Susana C."},{"family":"Magassouba","given":"Sékou"},{"family":"Morim","given":"Marli P."},{"family":"Mueller","given":"Gregory M."},{"family":"Nic Lughadha","given":"Eimear"},{"family":"Obreza","given":"Matija"},{"family":"Sharrock","given":"Suzanne"},{"family":"Simmonds","given":"Monique S. J."},{"family":"Tambam","given":"Beri Bonglim"},{"family":"Utteridge","given":"Timothy M. A."},{"family":"Breman","given":"Elinor"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2022",4,6]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020",9]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. The Millennium Seed Bank Partnership conserves high-quality propagules. It has involved 96 countries and territories, and 32% of taxa (representing half of the collections) have at least one identified use for humans ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a2h80n2utkn","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(U. Liu, Breman, Cossu, & Kenney, 2018)","plainCitation":"(U. Liu, Breman, Cossu, & Kenney, 2018)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31143,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/G4RC45A3"],"itemData":{"id":31143,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Biodiversity and Conservation","DOI":"10.1007/s10531-018-1497-y","ISSN":"0960-3115","issue":"6","journalAbbreviation":"Biodivers Conserv","language":"English","page":"1347-1386","title":"The conservation value of germplasm stored at the Millennium Seed Bank, Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew, UK","volume":"27","author":[{"family":"Liu","given":"U."},{"family":"Breman","given":"E."},{"family":"Cossu","given":"T. A."},{"family":"Kenney","given":"S."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018",5]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. 
      Regarding live wild plants gathering, analysis of the PlantSearch database hosted by Botanic Gardens Conservation International indicates that 107,340 accepted species grow in botanic garden collections, representing 31% of vascular plant species. However, 93% of these species are held in temperate parts of the world. As a result, a temperate species has a 60% chance of being cultivated within the botanic garden network, whereas a tropical species has only a 25% chance. 
      Collection for scientific purposes, however, is on the decline ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a287jrqqu2","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Heberling, Prather, & Tonsor, 2019)","plainCitation":"(Heberling, Prather, & Tonsor, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30887,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/MUT3543X"],"itemData":{"id":30887,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"BioScience","DOI":"10.1093/biosci/biz094","ISSN":"0006-3568","issue":"10","page":"812–822","title":"The Changing Uses of Herbarium Data in an Era of Global Change: An Overview Using Automated Content Analysis","volume":"69","author":[{"family":"Heberling","given":"J. Mason"},{"family":"Prather","given":"L. Alan"},{"family":"Tonsor","given":"Stephen J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, and there have been recent calls for more “holistic sampling” to maximize the usefulness of collections to protect individuals in the wild ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a2gm2f1ur0o","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Heberling, 2019; U. Liu, 2018)","plainCitation":"(Heberling, 2019; U. Liu, 2018)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30887,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/MUT3543X"],"itemData":{"id":30887,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"BioScience","DOI":"10.1093/biosci/biz094","ISSN":"0006-3568","issue":"10","page":"812–822","title":"The Changing Uses of Herbarium Data in an Era of Global Change: An Overview Using Automated Content Analysis","volume":"69","author":[{"family":"Heberling","given":"J. Mason"},{"family":"Prather","given":"L. Alan"},{"family":"Tonsor","given":"Stephen J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}},{"id":31143,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/G4RC45A3"],"itemData":{"id":31143,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Biodiversity and Conservation","DOI":"10.1007/s10531-018-1497-y","ISSN":"0960-3115","issue":"6","journalAbbreviation":"Biodivers Conserv","language":"English","page":"1347-1386","title":"The conservation value of germplasm stored at the Millennium Seed Bank, Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew, UK","volume":"27","author":[{"family":"Liu","given":"U."},{"family":"Breman","given":"E."},{"family":"Cossu","given":"T. A."},{"family":"Kenney","given":"S."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018",5]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Good photographs, non-lethal harvest techniques, and the sharing of specimen information or molecular methods ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a2nr6bo1krp","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Minteer, Collins, Love, & Puschendorf, 2014; D. Russo, Ancillotto, Hughes, Galimberti, & Mori, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Minteer, Collins, Love, & Puschendorf, 2014; D. Russo, Ancillotto, Hughes, Galimberti, & Mori, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31180,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/NSUIACBF"],"itemData":{"id":31180,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Science","DOI":"10.1126/science.1250953","ISSN":"0036-8075","issue":"6181","page":"260–261","title":"Avoiding (Re)extinction","volume":"344","author":[{"family":"Minteer","given":"B. A."},{"family":"Collins","given":"J. P."},{"family":"Love","given":"K. E."},{"family":"Puschendorf","given":"R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014"]]}}},{"id":31185,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/8FXQPGND"],"itemData":{"id":31185,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Mammal Review","DOI":"10.1111/mam.12095","ISSN":"0305-1838","issue":"4","page":"237–246","title":"Collection of voucher specimens for bat research: conservation, ethical implications, reduction, and alternatives","volume":"47","author":[{"family":"Russo","given":"Danilo"},{"family":"Ancillotto","given":"Leonardo"},{"family":"Hughes","given":"Alice C."},{"family":"Galimberti","given":"Andrea"},{"family":"Mori","given":"Emiliano"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} all represent good alternatives to lethal harvesting for scientific use. The Global Biodiversity Information Facility (GBIF) provides access to more than 1.4 billion records (including observations, preserved samples, fossils and living specimens) of all types of life on Earth in nearly 53,000 datasets supported by 1,600 institutions. The data of observation-based occurrences is surpassing the harvest of specimen-based occurrences in the Global Biodiversity Information Facility ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a2q6e3mt2tr","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Troudet, Vignes-Lebbe, Grandcolas, & Legendre, 2018)","plainCitation":"(Troudet, Vignes-Lebbe, Grandcolas, & Legendre, 2018)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31183,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/GT6628YX"],"itemData":{"id":31183,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Systematic Biology","DOI":"10.1093/sysbio/syy044","ISSN":"1063-5157","issue":"6","page":"1110–1119","title":"The Increasing Disconnection of Primary Biodiversity Data from Specimens: How Does It Happen and How to Handle It?","volume":"67","author":[{"family":"Troudet","given":"Julien"},{"family":"Vignes-Lebbe","given":"Régine"},{"family":"Grandcolas","given":"Philippe"},{"family":"Legendre","given":"Frédéric"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. However, African countries, Central, South and Southeast Asian countries and East European countries have been poorly represented in harvest of vascular plants species aggregated in the Global Biodiversity Information Facility and data in the World Checklist of Vascular Plants are also poor ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a25e38kl6lo","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Antonelli, 2020; Paton, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Antonelli, 2020; Paton, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id"