ess societal and environmental challenges. Collections also serve as a platform to engage and educate a broad range of stakeholders from the academic to the public, strengthening engagement and understanding of plant and fungal diversity—the basis of life on Earth.","container-title":"PLANTS, PEOPLE, PLANET","DOI":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ppp3.10141","issue":"5","page":"499-514","title":"Plant and fungal collections: Current status, future perspectives","volume":"2","author":[{"family":"Paton","given":"Alan"},{"family":"Antonelli","given":"Alexandre"},{"family":"Carine","given":"Mark"},{"family":"Forzza","given":"Rafaela Campostrini"},{"family":"Davies","given":"Nina"},{"family":"Demissew","given":"Sebsebe"},{"family":"Dröge","given":"Gabriele"},{"family":"Fulcher","given":"Tim"},{"family":"Grall","given":"Aurelie"},{"family":"Holstein","given":"Norbert"},{"family":"Jones","given":"Meirion"},{"family":"Liu","given":"Udayangani"},{"family":"Miller","given":"Joe"},{"family":"Moat","given":"Justin"},{"family":"Nicolson","given":"Nicky"},{"family":"Ryan","given":"Matthew"},{"family":"Sharrock","given":"Suzanne"},{"family":"Smith","given":"David"},{"family":"Thiers","given":"Barbara"},{"family":"Victor","given":"Janine"},{"family":"Wilkinson","given":"Tim"},{"family":"Dickie","given":"John"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}.
	Rocha ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a1e386vqugs","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(2014)","plainCitation":"(2014)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31146,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/TJT6IJ2A"],"itemData":{"id":31146,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Science","DOI":"10.1126/science.344.6186.814","ISSN":"1095-9203 (Electronic) 0036-8075 (Linking)","issue":"6186","language":"eng","page":"814-5","title":"Specimen collection: an essential tool","volume":"344","author":[{"family":"Rocha","given":"L. A."},{"family":"Aleixo","given":"A."},{"family":"Allen","given":"G."},{"family":"Almeda","given":"F."},{"family":"Baldwin","given":"C. C."},{"family":"Barclay","given":"M. V."},{"family":"Bates","given":"J. M."},{"family":"Bauer","given":"A. M."},{"family":"Benzoni","given":"F."},{"family":"Berns","given":"C. M."},{"family":"Berumen","given":"M. L."},{"family":"Blackburn","given":"D. C."},{"family":"Blum","given":"S."},{"family":"Bolanos","given":"F."},{"family":"Bowie","given":"R. C."},{"family":"Britz","given":"R."},{"family":"Brown","given":"R. M."},{"family":"Cadena","given":"C. D."},{"family":"Carpenter","given":"K."},{"family":"Ceriaco","given":"L. M."},{"family":"Chakrabarty","given":"P."},{"family":"Chaves","given":"G."},{"family":"Choat","given":"J. H."},{"family":"Clements","given":"K. D."},{"family":"Collette","given":"B. B."},{"family":"Collins","given":"A."},{"family":"Coyne","given":"J."},{"family":"Cracraft","given":"J."},{"family":"Daniel","given":"T."},{"family":"Carvalho","given":"M. R.","non-dropping-particle":"de"},{"family":"Queiroz","given":"K.","non-dropping-particle":"de"},{"family":"Di Dario","given":"F."},{"family":"Drewes","given":"R."},{"family":"Dumbacher","given":"J. P."},{"family":"Engilis","given":"A."},{"family":"Erdmann","given":"M. V."},{"family":"Eschmeyer","given":"W."},{"family":"Feldman","given":"C. R."},{"family":"Fisher","given":"B. L."},{"family":"Fjeldsa","given":"J."},{"family":"Fritsch","given":"P. W."},{"family":"Fuchs","given":"J."},{"family":"Getahun","given":"A."},{"family":"Gill","given":"A."},{"family":"Gomon","given":"M."},{"family":"Gosliner","given":"T."},{"family":"Graves","given":"G. R."},{"family":"Griswold","given":"C. E."},{"family":"Guralnick","given":"R."},{"family":"Hartel","given":"K."},{"family":"Helgen","given":"K. M."},{"family":"Ho","given":"H."},{"family":"Iskandar","given":"D. T."},{"family":"Iwamoto","given":"T."},{"family":"Jaafar","given":"Z."},{"family":"James","given":"H. F."},{"family":"Johnson","given":"D."},{"family":"Kavanaugh","given":"D."},{"family":"Knowlton","given":"N."},{"family":"Lacey","given":"E."},{"family":"Larson","given":"H. K."},{"family":"Last","given":"P."},{"family":"Leis","given":"J. M."},{"family":"Lessios","given":"H."},{"family":"Liebherr","given":"J."},{"family":"Lowman","given":"M."},{"family":"Mahler","given":"D. L."},{"family":"Mamonekene","given":"V."},{"family":"Matsuura","given":"K."},{"family":"Mayer","given":"G. C."},{"family":"Mays","given":"H."},{"family":"McCosker","given":"J."},{"family":"McDiarmid","given":"R. W."},{"family":"McGuire","given":"J."},{"family":"Miller","given":"M. J."},{"family":"Mooi","given":"R."},{"family":"Mooi","given":"R. D."},{"family":"Moritz","given":"C."},{"family":"Myers","given":"P."},{"family":"Nachman","given":"M. W."},{"family":"Nussbaum","given":"R. A."},{"family":"Foighil","given":"D. O."},{"family":"Parenti","given":"L. R."},{"family":"Parham","given":"J. F."},{"family":"Paul","given":"E."},{"family":"Paulay","given":"G."},{"family":"Perez-Eman","given":"J."},{"family":"Perez-Matus","given":"A."},{"family":"Poe","given":"S."},{"family":"Pogonoski","given":"J."},{"family":"Rabosky","given":"D. L."},{"family":"Randall","given":"J. E."},{"family":"Reimer","given":"J. D."},{"family":"Robertson","given":"D. R."},{"family":"Rodel","given":"M. O."},{"family":"Rodrigues","given":"M. T."},{"family":"Roopnarine","given":"P."},{"family":"Ruber","given":"L."},{"family":"Ryan","given":"M. J."},{"family":"Sheldon","given":"F."},{"family":"Shinohara","given":"G."},{"family":"Short","given":"A."},{"family":"Simison","given":"W. B."},{"family":"Smith-Vaniz","given":"W. F."},{"family":"Springer","given":"V. G."},{"family":"Stiassny","given":"M."},{"family":"Tello","given":"J. G."},{"family":"Thompson","given":"C. W."},{"family":"Trnski","given":"T."},{"family":"Tucker","given":"P."},{"family":"Valqui","given":"T."},{"family":"Vecchione","given":"M."},{"family":"Verheyen","given":"E."},{"family":"Wainwright","given":"P. C."},{"family":"Wheeler","given":"T. A."},{"family":"White","given":"W. T."},{"family":"Will","given":"K."},{"family":"Williams","given":"J. T."},{"family":"Williams","given":"G."},{"family":"Wilson","given":"E. O."},{"family":"Winker","given":"K."},{"family":"Winterbottom","given":"R."},{"family":"Witt","given":"C. C."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2014",5,23]]}},"suppress-author":true}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} have argued that halting the collection of voucher specimens by scientists would be detrimental. Scientists believe that in order to describe the earth's biodiversity and understand wild species, museum collections should increase by 600%, while still being collected responsibly following best practices ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"ai7denqq4p","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Henen, 2016)","plainCitation":"(Henen, 2016)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31182,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/98IZKVIE"],"itemData":{"id":31182,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Herpetol Conserv Biol","page":"13–18","title":"Do scientific collecting and conservation conflict","volume":"11","author":[{"family":"Henen","given":"Brian T."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Continued gathering would also support herbarium-based publications, which have dramatically increased in the past century ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a1jhfifngo9","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Heberling, 2019)","plainCitation":"(Heberling, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30887,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/MUT3543X"],"itemData":{"id":30887,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"BioScience","DOI":"10.1093/biosci/biz094","ISSN":"0006-3568","issue":"10","page":"812–822","title":"The Changing Uses of Herbarium Data in an Era of Global Change: An Overview Using Automated Content Analysis","volume":"69","author":[{"family":"Heberling","given":"J. Mason"},{"family":"Prather","given":"L. Alan"},{"family":"Tonsor","given":"Stephen J."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. To that end, regulatory authorities could develop quotas for specimen harvest that are based on scientific guidelines ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"ae3v9djhtl","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Maya & G\\\\uc0\\\\u243{}mez, 2016)","plainCitation":"(Maya & Gómez, 2016)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31178,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/CHS3F8CC"],"itemData":{"id":31178,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Journal of Insects as Food and Feed","DOI":"10.3920/jiff2015.0090","issue":"1","page":"43-52","title":"Insects and other invertebrates in the Pjiekakjoo (Tlahuica) culture in Mexico State, Mexico","volume":"2","author":[{"family":"Maya","given":"E. M. Aldasoro"},{"family":"Gómez","given":"B."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Scientific gathering practices also face a series of economic and social pressures, including budget cuts and shortfalls in university and museum settings ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a1d01jf4gvn","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Suarez & Tsutsui, 2004)","plainCitation":"(Suarez & Tsutsui, 2004)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31189,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/6STIBUUE"],"itemData":{"id":31189,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"BioScience","DOI":"10.1641/0006-3568(2004)054[0066:tvomcf]2.0.co;2","ISSN":"0006-3568","issue":"1","page":"66","title":"The Value of Museum Collections for Research and Society","volume":"54","author":[{"family":"Suarez","given":"ANDREW V."},{"family":"Tsutsui","given":"NEIL D."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2004"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, high gathering costs ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a2hef837lud","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Enrique, Daniela, & Fernando, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Enrique, Daniela, & Fernando, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31187,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/IHSBD5HX"],"itemData":{"id":31187,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Acta Biológica Colombiana","ISSN":"1900-1649","title":"On birds of Santander-Bio Expeditions, quantifying the cost of collecting voucher specimens in Colombia","volume":"25","author":[{"family":"Enrique","given":"Arbeláez-Cortés"},{"family":"Daniela","given":"Villamizar-Escalante"},{"family":"Fernando","given":"Rondón-González"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, ethical considerations, and effects of regulations like the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora for the cross-border exchange of specimens ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a14m33nec8k","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Roberts & Solow, 2008)","plainCitation":"(Roberts & Solow, 2008)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31177,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/JRHPVBX9"],"itemData":{"id":31177,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Proceedings. Biological sciences / The Royal Society","DOI":"10.1098/rspb.2007.1683","ISSN":"0962-8452","issue":"1637","page":"987–9","title":"The effect of the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species on scientific collections.","volume":"275","author":[{"family":"Roberts","given":"David L."},{"family":"Solow","given":"Andrew R."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2008"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. To promote scientific research on species conservation and materials sharing between scientists, the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora established the registered scientific institute scheme, and encourages Parties to register scientific institutes. So far, 74 Parties have registered a total of 857 scientific institutions and individuals with the Secretariat of the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"an3q3519g8","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Antonelli, 2020; C. Williams, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Antonelli, 2020; C. Williams, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30901,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/G9883U5U"],"itemData":{"id":30901,"type":"report","note":"DOI: 10.34885/172","publisher":"Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew","source":"DOI.org (Datacite)","title":"State of the World's Plants and Fungi 2020","URL":"https://kew.iro.bl.uk/work/23394899-864d-4ef0-b864-857efea500c5","author":[{"family":"Antonelli","given":"A."},{"family":"Fry","given":"C."},{"family":"Smith","given":"R.J."},{"family":"Simmonds","given":"M.S.J."},{"family":"Kersey","given":"P.J."},{"family":"Pritchard","given":"H.W."},{"family":"Abbo","given":"M.S."},{"family":"Acedo","given":"C."},{"family":"Adams","given":"J."},{"family":"Ainsworth","given":"A.M."},{"family":"Allkin","given":"B."},{"family":"Annecke","given":"W."},{"family":"Bachman","given":"S.P."},{"family":"Bacon","given":"K."},{"family":"Bárrios","given":"S."},{"family":"Barstow","given"