"},{"family":"Pérez Escobar","given":"O.A."},{"family":"Pieroni","given":"A."},{"family":"Pironon","given":"S."},{"family":"Prescott","given":"T.A.K."},{"family":"Qi","given":"Y.D."},{"family":"Qin","given":"H."},{"family":"Quave","given":"C.L."},{"family":"Rajaovelona","given":"L."},{"family":"Razanajatovo","given":"H."},{"family":"Reich","given":"P.B."},{"family":"Rianawati","given":"E."},{"family":"Rich","given":"T.C.G."},{"family":"Richards","given":"S.L."},{"family":"Rivers","given":"M.C."},{"family":"Ross","given":"A."},{"family":"Rumsey","given":"F."},{"family":"Ryan","given":"M."},{"family":"Ryan","given":"P."},{"family":"Sagala","given":"S."},{"family":"Sanchez","given":"M.D."},{"family":"Sharrock","given":"S."},{"family":"Shrestha","given":"K.K."},{"family":"Sim","given":"J."},{"family":"Sirakaya","given":"A."},{"family":"Sjöman","given":"H."},{"family":"Smidt","given":"E.C."},{"family":"Smith","given":"D."},{"family":"Smith","given":"P."},{"family":"Smith","given":"S.R."},{"family":"Sofo","given":"A."},{"family":"Spence","given":"N."},{"family":"Stanworth","given":"A."},{"family":"Stara","given":"K."},{"family":"Stevenson","given":"P.C."},{"family":"Stroh","given":"P."},{"family":"Suz","given":"L.M."},{"family":"Tambam","given":"B.B."},{"family":"Tatsis","given":"E.C."},{"family":"Taylor","given":"I."},{"family":"Thiers","given":"B."},{"family":"Thormann","given":"I."},{"family":"Vaglica","given":"V."},{"family":"Vásquez-Londoño","given":"C."},{"family":"Victor","given":"J."},{"family":"Viruel","given":"J."},{"family":"Walker","given":"B.E."},{"family":"Walker","given":"K."},{"family":"Walsh","given":"A."},{"family":"Way","given":"M."},{"family":"Wilbraham","given":"J."},{"family":"Wilkin","given":"P."},{"family":"Wilkinson","given":"T."},{"family":"Williams","given":"C."},{"family":"Winterton","given":"D."},{"family":"Wong","given":"K.M."},{"family":"Woodfield-Pascoe","given":"N."},{"family":"Woodman","given":"J."},{"family":"Wyatt","given":"L."},{"family":"Wynberg","given":"R."},{"family":"Zhang","given":"B.G."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",3,29]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020",9]]}}},{"id":30824,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/WZWSA42Z"],"itemData":{"id":30824,"type":"article-journal","abstract":"The wild relatives of domesticated crops possess genetic diversity useful for developing more productive, nutritious and resilient crop varieties. However, their conservation status and availability for utilization are a concern, and have not been quantified globally. Here, we model the global distribution of 1,076 taxa related to 81 crops, using occurrence information collected from biodiversity, herbarium and gene bank databases. We compare the potential geographic and ecological diversity encompassed in these distributions with that currently accessible in gene banks, as a means to estimate the comprehensiveness of the conservation of genetic diversity, Our results indicate that the diversity of crop wild relatives is poorly represented in gene banks. For 313 (29.1% of total) taxa associated with 63 crops, no germplasm accessions exist, and a further 257 (23.9%) are represented by fewer than ten accessions. Over 70% of taxa are identified as high priority for further collecting in order to improve their representation in gene banks, and over 95% are insufficiently represented in regard to the full range of geographic and ecological variation in their native distributions. The most critical collecting gaps occur in the Mediterranean and the Near East, western and southern Europe, Southeast and East Asia, and South America. We conclude that a systematic effort is needed to improve the conservation and availability of crop wild relatives for use in plant breeding. T he challenges to global food security are complex and compounding. Our growing population and changing dietary expectations are projected to increase demand on food systems for at least the next four decades 1 -5 , outpacing forecasted crop yield gains 6 . Limitations in land, water and other natural resource inputs, competition for arable soils with non-food crops and other land uses, soil degradation, climate change and the need to minimize harmful impacts on ecosystem services and biodiversity further constrain production potential 3 .4·7 ·8 . Although gains in food availability may partially be obtained through dietary change and food waste reduction 1 ·3 , increases in the productivity, resilience and sustainability of current agricultural systems are clearly necessary5. Key to this sustainable intensification","DOI":"10.1038/nplants.2016.22","issue":"April","page":"1-6","title":"Global conservation priorities for crop wild relatives","volume":"2","author":[{"family":"Castañeda-Álvarez","given":"Nora P"},{"family":"Khoury","given":"Colin K"},{"family":"Achicanoy","given":"Harold A"},{"family":"Bernau","given":"Vivian"},{"family":"Dempewolf","given":"Hannes"},{"family":"Eastwood","given":"Ruth J"},{"family":"Guarino","given":"Luigi"},{"family":"Harker","given":"Ruth H"},{"family":"Jarvis","given":"Andy"},{"family":"Maxted","given":"Nigel"},{"family":"Müller","given":"Jonas V"},{"family":"Ramirez-Villegas","given":"Julian"},{"family":"Sosa","given":"Chrystian C"},{"family":"Struik","given":"Paul C"},{"family":"Vincent","given":"Holly"},{"family":"Toll","given":"Jane"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}}},{"id":31164,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/ICUH5K9V"],"itemData":{"id":31164,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Biological Conservation","DOI":"10.1016/j.biocon.2013.08.011","ISSN":"00063207","journalAbbreviation":"Biological Conservation","language":"en","page":"265-275","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"A prioritized crop wild relative inventory to help underpin global food security","URL":"https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S0006320713002851","volume":"167","author":[{"family":"Vincent","given":"Holly"},{"family":"Wiersema","given":"John"},{"family":"Kell","given":"Shelagh"},{"family":"Fielder","given":"Hannah"},{"family":"Dobbie","given":"Samantha"},{"family":"Castañeda-Álvarez","given":"Nora P."},{"family":"Guarino","given":"Luigi"},{"family":"Eastwood","given":"Ruth"},{"family":"Le?n","given":"Blanca"},{"family":"Maxted","given":"Nigel"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2022",3,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013",11]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}.
      The Crop Wild Relatives Project (cwrdiversity.org) used the Harlan and de Wet (1971) gene pool concept to set up an inventory of globally important crop wild relatives' taxa for 173 priority crops. It contains 1667 taxa, divided between 37 families and 108 genera. The region with the highest number of priority crop wild relatives is Western Asia with 262 taxa, followed by China with 222 and Southeastern Europe with 181 ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a1cmi2srjpd","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Vincent, 2013)","plainCitation":"(Vincent, 2013)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31164,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/ICUH5K9V"],"itemData":{"id":31164,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Biological Conservation","DOI":"10.1016/j.biocon.2013.08.011","ISSN":"00063207","journalAbbreviation":"Biological Conservation","language":"en","page":"265-275","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"A prioritized crop wild relative inventory to help underpin global food security","URL":"https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S0006320713002851","volume":"167","author":[{"family":"Vincent","given":"Holly"},{"family":"Wiersema","given":"John"},{"family":"Kell","given":"Shelagh"},{"family":"Fielder","given":"Hannah"},{"family":"Dobbie","given":"Samantha"},{"family":"Castañeda-Álvarez","given":"Nora P."},{"family":"Guarino","given":"Luigi"},{"family":"Eastwood","given":"Ruth"},{"family":"Le?n","given":"Blanca"},{"family":"Maxted","given":"Nigel"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2022",3,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2013",11]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. However, the diversity of crop wild relatives is poorly represented in gene banks. Kew’s Millennium Seed Bank includes 688 crop wild relatives among its over 78,000 accessions. Over 70% of taxa are identified as high priority for further gathering in order to improve their representation in gene banks. The most critical gathering gaps occur in the Mediterranean and the Near East, Western and Southern Europe, Southeast and East Asia, and South America ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"SsqQanS9","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Antonelli, 2020; Casta\\\\uc0\\\\u241{}eda-\\\\uc0\\\\u193{}lvarez, 2016; Vincent, 2013)","plainCitation":"(Antonelli, 2020; Castañeda-Álvarez, 2016; Vincent, 2013)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":30901,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/G9883U5U"],"itemData":{"id":30901,"type":"report","note":"DOI: 10.34885/172","publisher":"Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew","source":"DOI.org (Datacite)","title":"State of the World's Plants and Fungi 2020","URL":"https://kew.iro.bl.uk/work/23394899-864d-4ef0-b864-857efea500c5","author":[{"family":"Antonelli","given":"A."},{"family":"Fry","given":"C."},{"family":"Smith","given":"R.J."},{"family":"Simmonds","given":"M.S.J."},{"family":"Kersey","given":"P.J."},{"family":"Pritchard","given":"H.W."},{"family":"Abbo","given":"M.S."},{"family":"Acedo","given":"C."},{"family":"Adams","given":"J."},{"family":"Ainsworth","given":"A.M."},{"family":"Allkin","given":"B."},{"family":"Annecke","given":"W."},{"family":"Bachman","given":"S.P."},{"family":"Bacon","given":"K."},{"family":"Bárrios","given":"S."},{"family":"Barstow","given":"C."},{"family":"Battison","given":"A."},{"family":"Bell","given":"E."},{"family":"Bensusan","given":"K."},{"family":"Bidartondo","given":"M.I."},{"family":"Blackhall-Miles","given":"R.J."},{"family":"Borrell","given":"J.S."},{"family":"Brearley","given":"F.Q."},{"family":"Breman","given":"E."},{"family":"Brewer","given":"R.F.A."},{"family":"Brodie","given":"J."},{"family":"Cámara-Leret","given":"R."},{"family":"Campostrini Forzza","given":"R."},{"family":"Cannon","given":"P."},{"family":"Carine","given":"M."},{"family":"Carretero","given":"J."},{"family":"Cavagnaro","given":"T.R."},{"family":"Cazar","given":"M.-E."},{"family":"Chapman","given":"T."},{"family":"Cheek","given":"M."},{"family":"Clubbe","given