ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a2m5ngcrl1f","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Di Minin, 2016)","plainCitation":"(Di Minin, 2016)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31079,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/VJBVT2C3"],"itemData":{"id":31079,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Trends in Ecology & Evolution","DOI":"10.1016/j.tree.2015.12.006","ISSN":"01695347","issue":"2","journalAbbreviation":"Trends in Ecology & Evolution","language":"en","page":"99-102","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Banning Trophy Hunting Will Exacerbate Biodiversity Loss","URL":"https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S0169534715003031","volume":"31","author":[{"family":"Di Minin","given":"Enrico"},{"family":"Leader-Williams","given":"Nigel"},{"family":"Bradshaw","given":"Corey J.A."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",2,27]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016",2]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}

      Prices paid for hunts vary from hundreds to hundreds of thousands of United States dollars (Table 3.15), and globally create a substantial revenue flow from developed to developing countries, as well as from urban to rural areas within countries ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"XtGk7L9p","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(V. R. Booth, 2010; Di Minin, 2016; IUCN, 2016; S\\\\uc0\\\\u225{}nchez-Garc\\\\uc0\\\\u237{}a, 2021)","plainCitation":"(V. R. Booth, 2010; Di Minin, 2016; IUCN, 2016; Sánchez-García, 2021)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31044,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/F5LN5LBJ"],"itemData":{"id":31044,"type":"report","collection-title":"CIC Technical Series Publication","event-place":"Budakeszi","language":"en","note":"OCLC: 741048011","number":"8","publisher":"FAO and CIC","publisher-place":"Budakeszi","source":"Open WorldCat","title":"Contribution of wildlife to national economies","URL":"https://www1.sun.ac.za/awei/sites/default/files/Technical_series_8.pdf","author":[{"family":"Booth","given":"Vernon R"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010"]]}}},{"id":31079,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/VJBVT2C3"],"itemData":{"id":31079,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Trends in Ecology & Evolution","DOI":"10.1016/j.tree.2015.12.006","ISSN":"01695347","issue":"2","journalAbbreviation":"Trends in Ecology & Evolution","language":"en","page":"99-102","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Banning Trophy Hunting Will Exacerbate Biodiversity Loss","URL":"https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S0169534715003031","volume":"31","author":[{"family":"Di Minin","given":"Enrico"},{"family":"Leader-Williams","given":"Nigel"},{"family":"Bradshaw","given":"Corey J.A."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",2,27]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016",2]]}}},{"id":30369,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/NP7U3IRZ"],"itemData":{"id":30369,"type":"report","abstract":"Trophy hunting is hunting of animals with specific desired characteristics (such as large antlers), and overlaps with widely practiced hunting for meat. ...","publisher":"IUCN","source":"Google Scholar","title":"Informing decisions on trophy hunting: A briefing paper for European Union decision-makers regarding potential plans for restriction of imports of hunting trophies","title-short":"Informing decisions on trophy hunting","URL":"https://www.iucn.org/sites/dev/files/iucn_sept_briefing_paper_-_informingdecisionstrophyhunting.pdf","author":[{"literal":"IUCN"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}}},{"id":1187,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/L4N29CGN"],"itemData":{"id":1187,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"International Journal of Environmental Studies","DOI":"10.1080/00207233.2020.1759305","ISSN":"0020-7233, 1029-0400","issue":"3","journalAbbreviation":"International Journal of Environmental Studies","language":"en","page":"517-531","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Evaluation of the economics of sport hunting in Spain through regional surveys","URL":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207233.2020.1759305","volume":"78","author":[{"family":"Sánchez-García","given":"Carlos"},{"family":"Urda","given":"Verónica"},{"family":"Lambarri","given":"María"},{"family":"Prieto","given":"Irene"},{"family":"Andueza","given":"Ana"},{"family":"Villanueva","given":"Luis F."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2022",3,19]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2021",5,4]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Besides spending money on hunting equipment, guns, ammunition, transportation, clothing, and meat processing, hunters typically also spend large amounts of money on permits, guide and outfitting services and travel ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a2lfmk6brkf","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(P. A. Lindsey, 2007; U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service, 2016)","plainCitation":"(P. A. Lindsey, 2007; U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service, 2016)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31039,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/ERD2GERZ"],"itemData":{"id":31039,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Biological Conservation","DOI":"10.1016/j.biocon.2006.09.005","ISSN":"00063207","issue":"4","journalAbbreviation":"Biological Conservation","language":"en","page":"455-469","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Economic and conservation significance of the trophy hunting industry in sub-Saharan Africa","URL":"https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S0006320706003831","volume":"134","author":[{"family":"Lindsey","given":"P.A."},{"family":"Roulet","given":"P.A."},{"family":"Romañach","given":"S.S."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",2,27]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2007",2]]}}},{"id":31053,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/YGDH4J5C"],"itemData":{"id":31053,"type":"report","title":"National Survey of Fishing, Hunting, and Wildlife-Associated Recreation","author":[{"family":"U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service","given":""}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, contributing to the economies of the areas where this practice occurs, for example, on communal conservancies in Namibia ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a2oji9vl14l","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(NACSO, 2015; NACSO & MET, 2018; Schmitt & Rempel, 2019)","plainCitation":"(NACSO, 2015; NACSO & MET, 2018; Schmitt & Rempel, 2019)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31102,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/KF3FM637"],"itemData":{"id":31102,"type":"document","abstract":"Every time we travel to a new place to visit, for fun or do a bit of work, we come back with memories, those we share or keep to ourselves. Here is my story, a tale I gathered while counting wildlife in conservancies of the North Eastern Namibia between the 4th and the 13th September 2015.","title":"Scary wildlife count in North East Namibia","URL":"http://www.nacso.org.na/news/2015/10/scary-wildlife-count-in-north-east-namibia","author":[{"family":"NACSO","given":""}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",3,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015",10,5]]}}},{"id":31051,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/KLZPU2Z8"],"itemData":{"id":31051,"type":"book","number-of-pages":"84","publisher":"Windhoek","title":"The State of Community Conservation in Namibia - a review of communal conservancies, community forests and other CBNRM initiatives","author":[{"family":"NACSO","given":""},{"family":"MET","given":""}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2018"]]}}},{"id":31047,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/JWMR6KVZ"],"itemData":{"id":31047,"type":"chapter","abstract":"Namibia’s hunting industry is increasingly threatened by animal rightists and opponent groups whose adversarial mindset is mostly based on emotion orientated information. The fatal consequences if closing hunting tourism in a country like Namibia are expounded in this study by critically investigating the input of well-regulated hunting tourism towards conservation in Namibia. Different factors have to be taken into consideration, regarding the country’s attributes that differ significantly from other countries and their methods to achieve successful conservation management strategies. By conducting an in-depth interview with Mr. Volker Grellmann and by obtaining secondary data from local authorities and organizations, the current research investigates how well-regulated hunting tourism in Namibia is an important part of biodiversity conservation. The results outline that hunting tourism is crucial for the value of wildlife and yields for wildlife to have a greater benefit than livestock and crop farming in Namibia. Likewise, the country takes care of their valuable natural recourse. As a result, natural habitats are induced, and subsequently a steeply growing number of wildlife was recorded over the last 50 years in Namibia. Among others hunting tourism favors the development of rural areas and yields incentives to fight poaching and the illegal trade of wild animal products. Published In: Bode, Freitag (Eds.): Universities, Entrepreneurship and Enterprise Development in Africa - Conference Proceedings 2018. Sankt Augustin, Germany, 13-14 September 2018","container-title":"Universities, Entrepreneurship and Enterprise Development in Africa","language":"en","page":"98-117","publisher":"German African University Partnership Platform for the Development of Entrepreneurs and Small/Medium Enterprises","source":"ideas.repec.org","title":"The Role of well-regulated Hunting Tourism in Namibia – in effective Conservation Management","URL":"https://ideas.repec.org/h/sau/ueedcc/07098-117.html","volume":"7","author":[{"family":"Schmitt","given":"Lisa"},{"family":"Rempel","given":"David"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",3,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2019"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. 
      
