      Shin, ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"xSjkFshZ","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(2017)","plainCitation":"(2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":483,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/4XJXLJX3"],"itemData":{"id":483,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Net. J. Agric. Sci","page":"53–57","title":"Paradigm shift on forest utilization: Forest service for health promotion in the Republic of Korea","URL":"http://www.netjournals.org/pdf/NJAS/2017/2/17-018.pdf","volume":"5","author":[{"family":"Shin","given":"Won Sop"},{"family":"Kim","given":"Jae-Jun"},{"family":"Lim","given":"Sang Seop"},{"family":"Yoo","given":"Rhee-Hwa"},{"family":"Jeong","given":"Mi-Ae"},{"family":"Lee","given":"Jeonghee"},{"family":"Park","given":"Sujin"},{"literal":"others"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",1,5]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}},"suppress-author":true}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} documented a significant increase in the use of Korean forests for recreational visitors, primarily for forest therapy and the health benefits of spending time in “healing forests”. This rise in health-based forest use has been facilitated by Korean government forests restoration programs, legislating certain forests specifically as “healing forests”, and substantial investment in forest therapy research ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"tQrM6tGl","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Shin, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Shin, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":483,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/4XJXLJX3"],"itemData":{"id":483,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Net. J. Agric. Sci","page":"53–57","title":"Paradigm shift on forest utilization: Forest service for health promotion in the Republic of Korea","URL":"http://www.netjournals.org/pdf/NJAS/2017/2/17-018.pdf","volume":"5","author":[{"family":"Shin","given":"Won Sop"},{"family":"Kim","given":"Jae-Jun"},{"family":"Lim","give