      A drawback of environmental education is the limited reach of the programs. Although some ripple effect in increased awareness in the community ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"S1MtKCkq","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Vaughan, 2003)","plainCitation":"(Vaughan, 2003)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31690,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/MHBAD2FA"],"itemData":{"id":31690,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"The Journal of Environmental Education","DOI":"10.1080/00958960309603489","ISSN":"0095-8964, 1940-1892","issue":"3","journalAbbreviation":"The Journal of Environmental Education","language":"en","page":"12-21","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"The Effect of Environmental Education on Schoolchildren, Their Parents, and Community Members: A Study of Intergenerational and Intercommunity Learning","title-short":"The Effect of Environmental Education on Schoolchildren, Their Parents, and Community Members","URL":"http://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/00958960309603489","volume":"34","author":[{"family":"Vaughan","given":"Christopher"},{"family":"Gack","given":"Julie"},{"family":"Solorazano","given":"Humberto"},{"family":"Ray","given":"Robert"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",1,8]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2003",1]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, in communities reliant on natural resources and living in vulnerable ecosystems, it is the children who do not attend school who are more likely to be involved in illegal and unsustainable wild species activities in the future ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"9JjGaW55","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Breuer & Mavinga, 2010)","plainCitation":"(Breuer & Mavinga, 2010)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31693,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/QU73HTA8"],"itemData":{"id":31693,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"American Journal of Primatology","DOI":"10.1002/ajp.20774","ISSN":"02752565","issue":"5","journalAbbreviation":"Am. J. Primatol.","language":"en","page":"454-461","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Education for the conservation of great apes and other wildlife in northern Congo-the importance of nature clubs","URL":"http://doi.wiley.com/10.1002/ajp.20774","volume":"72","author":[{"family":"Breuer","given":"Thomas"},{"family":"Mavinga","given":"Franck Barrel"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",1,8]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010",5]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Furthermore, education alone cannot be solely responsible for changes in behavior. Environmental education programs need to be complemented by projects that alleviate poverty and develop alternative livelihood opportunities ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"tJVQaMD5","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Breuer & Mavinga, 2010)","plainCitation":"(Breuer & Mavinga, 2010)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31693,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/QU73HTA8"],"itemData":{"id":31693,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"American Journal of Primatology","DOI":"10.1002/ajp.20774","ISSN":"02752565","issue":"5","journalAbbreviation":"Am. J. Primatol.","language":"en","page":"454-461","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Education for the conservation of great apes and other wildlife in northern Congo-the importance of nature clubs","URL":"http://doi.wiley.com/10.1002/ajp.20774","volume":"72","author":[{"family":"Breuer","given":"Thomas"},{"family":"Mavinga","given":"Franck Barrel"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",1,8]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2010",5]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. Conservationists and local governments should also provide information on the importance of ecological functions of wild species that cause problems in human-wildlife conflict, whilst mitigating the drawbacks of close contact with ‘problematic’ species ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"u4qh54H4","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Hosaka, Sugimoto, & Numata, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Hosaka, Sugimoto, & Numata, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31681,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/KUAADWSM"],"itemData":{"id":31681,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"PLOS ONE","DOI":"10.1371/journal.pone.0175243","ISSN":"1932-6203","issue":"4","journalAbbreviation":"PLoS ONE","language":"en","page":"e0175243","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Effects of childhood experience with nature on tolerance of urban residents toward hornets and wild boars in Japan","URL":"https://dx.plos.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0175243","volume":"12","author":[{"family":"Hosaka","given":"Tetsuro"},{"family":"Sugimoto","given":"Koun"},{"family":"Numata","given":"Shinya"}],"editor":[{"family":"Ito","given":"Etsuro"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",1,8]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017",4,7]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}.
      
