","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Spenceley, 2021)","plainCitation":"(Spenceley, 2021)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":441,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/M7STDQP8"],"itemData":{"id":441,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"PARKS","DOI":"10.2305/IUCN.CH.2021.PARKS-27-SIAS.en","ISSN":"0960233X","issue":"27","journalAbbreviation":"PARKS","page":"103-118","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Tourism in protected and conserved areas amid the COVID-19 pandemic","URL":"https://parksjournal.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Spenceley_et_al10.2305-IUCN.CH_.2021.PARKS-27-SIAS.en_.pdf","author":[{"family":"Spenceley","given":"Anna"},{"family":"McCool","given":"Steve"},{"family":"Newsome","given":"David"},{"family":"Báez","given":"Ana"},{"family":"Barborak","given":"James R."},{"family":"Blye","given":"Clara-Jane"},{"family":"Bricker","given":"Kelly"},{"family":"Sigit Cahyadi","given":"Hery"},{"family":"Corrigan","given":"Katherine"},{"family":"Halpenny","given":"Elizabeth"},{"family":"Hvenegaard","given":"Glen"},{"family":"Malleret King","given":"Delphine"},{"family":"Leung","given":"Yu-Fai"},{"family":"Mandi?","given":"Ante"},{"family":"Naidoo","given":"Robin"},{"family":"Rüede","given":"Dominik"},{"family":"Sano","given":"James"},{"family":"Sarhan","given":"Mahmoud"},{"family":"Santamaria","given":"Veronica"},{"family":"Beraldo Sousa","given":"Thiago"},{"family":"Zschiegner","given":"Anne-Kathrin"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",9,21]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2021",3,11]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}, compounded by the return of migrant workers to rural areas and the associated increase in demand of local resources ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"2IXNG3Tc","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Rondeau, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Rondeau, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31647,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/FA9IIB7T"],"itemData":{"id":31647,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Environmental and Resource Economics","DOI":"10.1007/s10640-020-00480-7","ISSN":"0924-6460, 1573-1502","issue":"4","journalAbbreviation":"Environ Resource Econ","language":"en","page":"945-961","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"The Consequences of COVID-19 and Other Disasters for Wildlife and Biodiversity","URL":"https://link.springer.com/10.1007/s10640-020-00480-7","volume":"76","author":[{"family":"Rondeau","given":"Daniel"},{"family":"Perry","given":"Brianna"},{"family":"Grimard","given":"Franque"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",9,21]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020",8]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. There are preliminary indications of increase poaching and a surge in illegal logging during the pandemic, possibly as a result of decreased conservation authority presence and no wildlife watching tourists ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"V3RcsfYY","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Rondeau, 2020; Spenceley, 2021)","plainCitation":"(Rondeau, 2020; Spenceley, 2021)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31647,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/FA9IIB7T"],"itemData":{"id":31647,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Environmental and Resource Economics","DOI":"10.1007/s10640-020-00480-7","ISSN":"0924-6460, 1573-1502","issue":"4","journalAbbreviation":"Environ Resource Econ","language":"en","page":"945-961","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"The Consequences of COVID-19 and Other Disasters for Wildlife and Biodiversity","URL":"https://link.springer.com/10.1007/s10640-020-00480-7","volume":"76","author":[{"family":"Rondeau","given":"Daniel"},{"family":"Perry","given":"Brianna"},{"family":"Grimard","given":"Franque"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",9,21]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020",8]]}}},{"id":441,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/M7STDQP8"],"itemData":{"id":441,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"PARKS","DOI":"10.2305/IUCN.CH.2021.PARKS-27-SIAS.en","ISSN":"0960233X","issue":"27","journalAbbreviation":"PARKS","page":"103-118","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Tourism in protected and conserved areas amid the COVID-19 pandemic","URL":"https://parksjournal.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Spenceley_et_al10.2305-IUCN.CH_.2021.PARKS-27-SIAS.en_.pdf","author":[{"family":"Spenceley","given":"Anna"},{"family":"McCool","given":"Steve"},{"family":"Newsome","given":"David"},{"family":"Báez","given":"Ana"},{"family":"Barborak","given":"James R."},{"family":"Blye","given":"Clara-Jane"},{"family":"Bricker","given":"Kelly"},{"family":"Sigit Cahyadi","given":"Hery"},{"family":"Corrigan","given":"Katherine"},{"family":"Halpenny","given":"Elizabeth"},{"family":"Hvenegaard","given":"Glen"},{"family":"Malleret King","given":"Delphine"},{"family":"Leung","given":"Yu-Fai"},{"family":"Mandi?","given":"Ante"},{"family":"Naidoo","given":"Robin"},{"family":"Rüede","given":"Dominik"},{"family":"Sano","given":"James"},{"family":"Sarhan","given":"Mahmoud"},{"family":"Santamaria","given":"Veronica"},{"family":"Beraldo Sousa","given":"Thiago"},{"family":"Zschiegner","given":"Anne-Kathrin"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",9,21]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2021",3,11]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. In addition to the lack of tourism revenue, it is unknown what the impacts of COVID-19 transmission from tourists on wild species will be ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"iUrlQ3ZF","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(A. Gibbons, 2020)","plainCitation":"(A. Gibbons, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31648,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/EEKNHQ53"],"itemData":{"id":31648,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Science","DOI":"10.1126/science.368.6491.566-a","ISSN":"0036-8075, 1095-9203","issue":"6491","journalAbbreviation":"Science","language":"en","page":"566.1-566","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"Ape researchers mobilize to save primates from coronavirus","URL":"https://www.sciencemag.org/lookup/doi/10.1126/science.368.6491.566-a","volume":"368","author":[{"family":"Gibbons","given":"Ann"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",9,21]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020",5,8]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} or from tourists to local communities ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"a1up28d7ojl","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Hakim, 2020)","plainCitation":"(Hakim, 2020)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":31630,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/S2SAB4SC"],"itemData":{"id":31630,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Journal of Marine and Island Cultures","DOI":"10.21463/jmic.2020.09.1.08","ISSN":"22126821","issue":"1","journalAbbreviation":"JMIC","source":"DOI.org (Crossref)","title":"COVID-19, tourism, and small islands in Indonesia: Protecting fragile communities in the global Coronavirus pandemic","title-short":"COVID-19, tourism, and small islands in Indonesia","URL":"https://jmic.online/issues/v9n1/8/","volume":"9","author":[{"family":"Hakim","given":"Luchman"}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2021",12,14]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020",6,29]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}. But these early findings still need to be corroborated with more data as the effects of the pandemic on wild species, conservation funds, and local livelihoods becomes more understood.
      Another emerging issue is the non-extractive use of wild species through novel finance mechanisms, such as Rhino Impact Bonds (www.rhinoimpact.com), Lion Carbon (www.lionlandscapes.org/lioncarbon), The Lion’s Share Fund (www.thelionssharefund.com), or the Luc Hoffmann Institute’s Innovation Challenge “Beyond Tourism in Africa” (https://luchoffmanninstitute.org/beyond-tourism-in-africa-innovation-challenge) which seek to support wild species conservation and sustainable livelihoods in the absence of recreational hunting or wildlife tourism. However, there is currently insufficient information on the use, trends or impacts of these finance mechanisms on wild species or wildlife economies.

