5)","plainCitation":"(Ayala-Burbano, 2020; Drury, 2016; Xue, 2015)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":32878,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/34ZYI976"],"itemData":{"id":32878,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Scientific Reports","language":"en","page":"11","source":"Zotero","title":"Studbook and molecular analyses for the endangered black-lion-tamarin; an integrative approach for assessing genetic diversity and driving management in captivity","volume":"10:6781","author":[{"family":"Ayala-Burbano","given":"Paola Andrea"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2020"]]}}},{"id":32895,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/MGSVU76A"],"itemData":{"id":32895,"type":"article-journal","abstract":"Acropora cervicornis, a threatened, keystone reef-building coral has undergone severe declines (>90 %) throughout the Caribbean. These declines could reduce genetic variation and thus hamper the species’ ability to adapt. Active restoration strategies are a common conservation approach to mitigate species' declines and require genetic data on surviving populations to efficiently respond to declines while maintaining the genetic diversity needed to adapt to changing conditions. To evaluate active restoration strategies for the staghorn coral, the genetic diversity of A. cervicornis within and among populations was assessed in 77 individuals collected from 68 locations along the Florida Reef Tract (FRT) and in the Dominican Republic.","container-title":"BMC Genomics","DOI":"10.1186/s12864-016-2583-8","ISSN":"1471-2164","issue":"1","journalAbbreviation":"BMC Genomics","page":"286","source":"BioMed Central","title":"Genomic variation among populations of threatened coral: Acropora cervicornis","title-short":"Genomic variation among populations of threatened coral","URL":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12864-016-2583-8","volume":"17","author":[{"family":"Drury","given":"C."},{"family":"Dale","given":"K. E."},{"family":"Panlilio","given":"J. M."},{"family":"Miller","given":"S. V."},{"family":"Lirman","given":"D."},{"family":"Larson","given":"E. A."},{"family":"Bartels","given":"E."},{"family":"Crawford","given":"D. L."},{"family":"Oleksiak","given":"M. F."}],"accessed":{"date-parts":[["2019",7,25]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[["2016",4,13]]}}},{"id":32815,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/YVIPUSN5"],"itemData":{"id":32815,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Science. April","issue":"6231","language":"en","page":"242–245","title":"Mountain gorilla genomes reveal the impact of long-term population decline and inbreeding","volume":"10","author":[{"family":"Xue","given":"Y."}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2015"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"} and the critical role of pollinators ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"DFXvSJjR","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Lopez-Maldonado & Berkes, 2017)","plainCitation":"(Lopez-Maldonado & Berkes, 2017)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":32835,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/K9JWVAU9"],"itemData":{"id":32835,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Ecology and Society","issue":"4","language":"en","title":"Restoring the Environment, Revitalizing the Culture: Cenote Conservation in Yucatan, Mexico","volume":"22","author":[{"family":"Lopez-Maldonado","given":"Yolanda"},{"family":"Berkes","given":"Fikret"}],"issued":{"date-parts":[["2017"]]}}}],"schema":"https://github.com/citation-style-language/schema/raw/master/csl-citation.json"}; monitor environmental change ITEM CSL_CITATION {"citationID":"uZ6hj906","properties":{"formattedCitation":"(Thomsen & Willerslev, 2015)","plainCitation":"(Thomsen & Willerslev, 2015)","noteIndex":0},"citationItems":[{"id":33100,"uris":["http://zotero.org/groups/2344805/items/5UVCGN53"],"itemData":{"id":33100,"type":"article-journal","container-title":"Biological Conservation","language":"en","page":"4–18","title":"Environmental DNA – An emerging tool in conservation for